∇Z←dm∆DTWPredecessor
⍝ Selected predecessor of an actual positive DTW cell. advance_a changes the first coordinate, advance_b the second. Finite ties prefer diagonal, then advance_a, then advance_b. Unrepresentable accumulated costs have no finite predecessor witness; successful traceback never uses them.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1},{1});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",t.predecessors[0]==dm::geometry::DTWPredecessor::origin); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:** `Z←dm∆DTWPredecessor` (a 2-column matrix: names, values). Each enumerator is a niladic function:
⍝ - `dm∆DTWPredecessor∆origin` = 0
⍝ - `dm∆DTWPredecessor∆diagonal` = 1
⍝ - `dm∆DTWPredecessor∆advance_a` = 2
⍝ - `dm∆DTWPredecessor∆advance_b` = 3
⍝ - `dm∆DTWPredecessor∆unrepresentable` = 4
⍝
⍝ Enumerators are numbers; functions also accept their names as character vectors.
⍝
⍝ - C++: `enum class datamunge::geometry::DTWPredecessor`
 Z←5 2⍴(,'origin') 0 (,'diagonal') 1 (,'advance_a') 2 (,'advance_b') 3 (,'unrepresentable') 4
