∇Z←dm∆Expr∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A symbolic expression tree over +, -, *, /, ^ (power) and sin/cos/exp/log, supporting symbolic differentiation, basic algebraic simplification, and numeric evaluation. Value type wrapping a shared, immutable node tree -- copies are cheap and structural sharing across copies is always safe since nodes are never mutated after construction.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆Expr∆constant` (static), `dm∆Expr∆variable` (static), `dm∆Expr∆add`, `dm∆Expr∆subtract`, `dm∆Expr∆multiply`, `dm∆Expr∆divide`, `dm∆Expr∆power`, `dm∆Expr∆negate`, `dm∆Expr∆sin`, `dm∆Expr∆cos`, `dm∆Expr∆exp`, `dm∆Expr∆log`, `dm∆Expr∆differentiate`, `dm∆Expr∆integrate`, `dm∆Expr∆simplify`, `dm∆Expr∆evaluate`, `dm∆Expr∆to_string`, `dm∆Expr∆to_tex`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('Expr' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆Expr∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆Expr∆new value
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Construct a symbolic constant from a C++ numeric value, including implicit conversion.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Expr handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - WS FULL `dm: allocation: …`: If the constant node cannot be allocated. (C++ `std::bad_alloc`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::algebra::Expr::Expr()`
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::algebra::Expr::Expr(double value)`
