∇Z←dm∆HMC∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Hamiltonian Monte Carlo with a fixed leapfrog trajectory length and Nesterov dual-averaging step-size adaptation during warmup (Hoffman & Gelman 2014), using an identity mass matrix. Samples from the distribution proportional to exp(log_posterior) over unconstrained real parameters.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆HMC∆sample`, `dm∆HMC∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('HMC' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆HMC∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆HMC∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Stores the sampler settings.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` HMCOptions handle, default the C++ default: Sampler settings.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** HMC handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::bayes::HMC::HMC(HMCOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 423) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

