∇Z←dm∆ImportanceSampling∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Importance sampling against a multivariate Gaussian proposal N(mean, covariance) -- a natural choice when a Laplace approximation is available and reasonably close to the target's shape (e.g. bayes::MAP's mode paired with a numerically estimated Hessian there). Produces a weighted i.i.d. sample in one shot rather than a Markov chain -- no warmup, nothing to check for mixing -- but accuracy depends entirely on how well the Gaussian proposal covers the target's mass; effective_sample_size is the diagnostic to check before trusting the result.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ImportanceSampling∆sample`, `dm∆ImportanceSampling∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ImportanceSampling' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ImportanceSampling∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆ImportanceSampling∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Stores the sampler settings.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` ImportanceSamplingOptions handle, default the C++ default: Sampler settings.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ImportanceSampling handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::bayes::ImportanceSampling::ImportanceSampling(ImportanceSamplingOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 440) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆ImportanceSampling∆sample B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ `log_target` need only be evaluable (optim::ArbitraryFunction), not differentiable. `proposal_covariance` (a plain d x d nested vector, not linalg::DenseMatrix -- matrices never cross the SWIG boundary as DenseMatrix anywhere in this library, only as nested vectors) must be symmetric positive definite.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆ImportanceSampling∆sample log_target proposal_mean proposal_covariance
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `log_target` ArbitraryFunction handle
⍝ - `proposal_mean` numeric vector
⍝ - `proposal_covariance` numeric matrix (one row per element)
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ImportanceSamplingResult handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `ImportanceSamplingResult datamunge::bayes::ImportanceSampling::sample(optim::ArbitraryFunction & log_target, const std::vector<double> & proposal_mean, const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & proposal_covariance) const`
