∇Z←dm∆NUTS∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The No-U-Turn Sampler (Hoffman & Gelman 2014, the efficient slice-sampling variant, Algorithm 3): Hamiltonian Monte Carlo with an automatically chosen trajectory length -- the leapfrog trajectory is grown by repeated doubling until it would start turning back on itself (a "U-turn"), removing the need to hand-tune a fixed number of leapfrog steps. Step size is still adapted via the same dual-averaging scheme as HMC. Uses an identity mass matrix.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆NUTS∆sample`, `dm∆NUTS∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('NUTS' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆NUTS∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆NUTS∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Stores the sampler settings.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` NUTSOptions handle, default the C++ default: Sampler settings.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** NUTS handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::bayes::NUTS::NUTS(NUTSOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 485) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

