∇Z←dm∆RWMOptions∆adapt_covariance H;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Learn a proposal covariance during warmup (adaptive Metropolis, Haario et al. 2001). The first half of warmup is isotropic; at its end the covariance
⍝
⍝ `\hat\Sigma` of the second quarter's draws, shrunk slightly towards
⍝ `10^{-3}I`, becomes the proposal shape `x'=x+\varepsilon Lz` with
⍝ `LL^\top=\hat\Sigma`, and the step size is re-adapted from
⍝ `\varepsilon=2.38/\sqrt d` for the rest of warmup.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:** `Z←dm∆RWMOptions∆adapt_covariance obj`; set it with `obj dm∆RWMOptions∆adapt_covariance∆set value`
⍝
⍝ **Result:** boolean (0 or 1)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `bool datamunge::bayes::RWMOptions::adapt_covariance`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(496 2 H) dm⍙native ⍬
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

