∇Z←dm∆Image∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A 2D raster image: row-major, top-left origin, interleaved channel bytes (matching the layout every common image codec uses on disk, so I/O needs no reshuffling). Pixel data is always stored as the mode's exact channel count (1/2/3/4 bytes per pixel) -- get_pixel()/set_pixel() are the only place mode-specific expansion happens.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆Image∆width`, `dm∆Image∆height`, `dm∆Image∆mode`, `dm∆Image∆channels`, `dm∆Image∆data`, `dm∆Image∆get_pixel`, `dm∆Image∆set_pixel`, `dm∆Image∆fill`, `dm∆Image∆channel_count` (static).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('Image' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆Image∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆Image∆new width height
⍝ obj←dm∆Image∆new width height mode
⍝ obj←dm∆Image∆new width height mode fill_color
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Image handle
