∇Z←dm∆ImageLoader∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A configurable, disk-backed batch iterator over a standard image dataset.
⍝
⍝ Datasets: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" (28x28 grayscale, 10 classes; 60000 train / 10000
⍝ test), "cifar10" (32x32 RGB, 10 classes; 50000 / 10000) and "cifar100" (32x32 RGB, 100 fine
⍝ or 20 coarse classes; 50000 / 10000).
⍝
⍝ Iteration works in epochs. has_next()/next() walk the current epoch's order; reset() starts
⍝ the next epoch (with a fresh shuffle when shuffling is on). Every setter returns the loader
⍝ for chaining and rewinds the current epoch, so configure before iterating.
⍝
⍝ Reading is const and opens files per call, so batch()/take() may be called from several
⍝ threads at once; next()/reset() and the setters mutate and must not race.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::datasets::ImageLoader test("cifar10", "test");
⍝ test.set_batch_size(500).set_layout("nchw").set_normalize(false);
⍝ const auto first = test.next();          // shape {500, 3, 32, 32}, values 0..255
⍝ std::print("{}\n", test.class_names()[first.labels[0]]);   // "cat"
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_batch_size`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_shuffle`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_seed`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_drop_last`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_normalize`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_layout`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_limit`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆set_coarse_labels`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆dataset`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆split`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆directory`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆batch_size`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆shuffle`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆seed`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆drop_last`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆normalize`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆layout`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆coarse_labels`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆size`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆split_size`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆num_batches`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆height`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆width`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆channels`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆num_classes`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆class_names`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆epoch`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆position`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆has_next`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆next`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆reset`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆batch`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆take`, `dm∆ImageLoader∆load_all`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ImageLoader' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ImageLoader∆new dataset
⍝ obj←dm∆ImageLoader∆new dataset split
⍝ obj←dm∆ImageLoader∆new dataset split directory
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Opens a dataset split, downloading the files first if they are missing.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `dataset` character vector: "mnist", "fashion_mnist", "cifar10" or "cifar100".
⍝ - `split` character vector, default 'train': "train" or "test".
⍝ - `directory` character vector, default '': Where the dataset's files are (or should be downloaded); empty means `data_home() + "/" + dataset`.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ImageLoader handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
