∇Z←dm∆BoundaryCondition1D∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned endpoint data for Dirichlet, outward-conormal Neumann or Robin conditions. Dirichlet uses value as u; Neumann uses it as p*du/dn; Robin uses it as the reference value in p*du/dn+alpha*(u-value)=0. Alpha zero gives zero conormal. For coercive diffusion/heat models use nonnegative Robin alpha and sufficient constraints/reaction to remove the constant nullspace. Unsupported enum values and nonfinite data are outside the solver's preconditions, not fully validated.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const dm::fem::BoundaryCondition1D right{dm::fem::BCType::Robin,4,3};
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n",right.value,right.robin_coefficient); // 4 3
⍝ ```
