∇Z←dm∆FEM1DResult∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned nodal P1 steady solution, with checked scalar accessors for language bindings. The continuous finite-element field is the piecewise-linear interpolant of these values; nodal agreement alone does not imply agreement between nodes. Copies own their arrays, with no mesh/callback alias. Public edits can break array consistency; accessors check the actual requested vector bounds.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{});
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n",r.size(),r.value_at(1)); // 3 0.125
⍝ ```
