∇Z←dm∆FEM1DTimeSeries∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned initial state and actual strictly advancing backward-Euler time slices. Solver output has one u row per time and one value per spatial node. Initial time zero/u0 are retained as supplied; later rows satisfy imposed boundary data. Times retain rounded nominal-step products with a shortened final interval; an already reached endpoint is not appended twice. Copies retain no mesh/source alias. Public edits may break consistency; accessors check actual vector bounds.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{},{0,0,0},.5,.5);
⍝ std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2 0.107143
⍝ ```
⍝
