∇Z←dm∆FEM1D∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Solve steady or transient one-dimensional divergence-form problems with P1 Galerkin FEM. Models -(p*u')'+q*u=f and u_t-(p*u')'+q*u=f on a caller-supplied mesh. Requires at least two finite strictly increasing nodes, finite coefficient/ boundary/source data and finite assembled arithmetic with nonzero Thomas pivots; those mathematical/geometry preconditions are not fully validated. Positive p, nonnegative q/Robin data and adequate constraints give the usual coercive model. Piecewise-constant p/q can be scalar or one per element. Results own their values; input mesh/data are unchanged. Calls share no mutable global state, while callback side effects/concurrency belong to the caller.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - MFEM, Weak Formulations: https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ . This native implementation
⍝   uses P1 intervals, three-point Gauss-Legendre loads and a tridiagonal direct solve.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆FEM1D∆solve` (static), `dm∆FEM1D∆solve_builtin` (static), `dm∆FEM1D∆solve_transient` (static), `dm∆FEM1D∆solve_transient_builtin` (static).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('FEM1D' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆FEM1D∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** FEM1D handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::fem::FEM1D::FEM1D()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 2 669) dm⍙native ⍬
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Solve the steady P1 system for -(p*u')'+q*u=f with endpoint boundary data. Follows FEM1D's mesh/coefficient/finite-arithmetic/nonsingular-pivot preconditions. Uses three-point Gauss-Legendre quadrature of f times each local basis, natural boundary terms and symmetric Dirichlet elimination, then Thomas elimination. O(N) work/storage for N nodes; invokes the source three times per element. No callback pointer is retained. Independent calls share no mutable state.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ struct Unit final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double evaluate(double) override{return 1;}} source;
⍝ const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; native interval P1 and quadrature choices as FEM1D.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve mesh p q f left right
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `mesh` Mesh1D handle: Borrowed mesh with at least two finite strictly increasing nodes.
⍝ - `p` numeric vector: Borrowed diffusion coefficient: length1 or one per element.
⍝ - `q` numeric vector: Borrowed reaction coefficient: length1 or one per element.
⍝ - `f` ScalarField1D handle: Borrowed spatial source; evaluate() may have caller-owned side effects.
⍝ - `left` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Left endpoint condition, with outward normal -1.
⍝ - `right` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Right endpoint condition, with outward normal +1.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** FEM1DResult handle: Owned original nodes and computed nodal values.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If p/q are empty or have the wrong lengths. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - WS FULL `dm: allocation: …`: If assembly/result storage cannot be allocated; callback exceptions propagate. (C++ `std::bad_alloc`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `FEM1DResult datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const std::vector<double> & q, ScalarField1D & f, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆solve_builtin()`, `dm∆solve_transient()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(665 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve_builtin B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Solve the steady system using an owned named spatial source, without a director callback. Shares the live-source solver and its mathematical/precondition/storage contracts. Sources: zero=0 (params unused); constant=c ({1}); linear=m*x+c ({1,0}); polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty gives0); sine=A*sin(w*x+phase) ({1,1,0}). Missing trailing parameters use those defaults; extra parameters are ignored except polynomial, which uses all entries. Name matching is exact/case-sensitive.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{}, {},{});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; source definitions are native convenience choices.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve_builtin mesh p q source source_params left right
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `mesh` Mesh1D handle: Borrowed valid finite interval mesh; unchanged.
⍝ - `p` numeric vector: Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
⍝ - `q` numeric vector: Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
⍝ - `source` character vector: Exact name zero, constant, linear, polynomial or sine.
⍝ - `source_params` numeric vector: Borrowed positional source parameters, with defaults described above.
⍝ - `left` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Left endpoint data using outward normal -1.
⍝ - `right` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Right endpoint data using outward normal +1.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** FEM1DResult handle: Owned computed nodal result, retaining no source or input reference.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: For an unknown source or malformed p/q lengths. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - WS FULL `dm: allocation: …`: If owned parameter/assembly/result storage cannot be allocated. (C++ `std::bad_alloc`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `FEM1DResult datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const std::vector<double> & q, const std::string & source, const std::vector<double> & source_params, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆solve()`, `dm∆solve_transient_builtin()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(666 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve_transient B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Integrate u_t-(p*u')'+q*u=f with P1 space and actual backward-Euler time intervals. Shares FEM1D's spatial/finite-arithmetic/nonzero-pivot preconditions. Source and boundary data represent a time-independent model; the live callback is actually reevaluated three times per element at every time advance, not cached. Stores initial u0 as supplied, then imposes boundary data at later solves. Nominal step dt is shortened at t_end; actual positive time differences enter the mass term. Stops once t_end is reached, avoiding a duplicate rounded last time even when ceil(t_end/dt) overestimates the number of advances. O(S*N) work/output storage for S advances/N nodes, O(N) assembly temporaries; no optional trace or quota. Backward Euler is unconditionally stable for the coercive semidiscrete model, not a guarantee of arbitrary-step accuracy or finite arithmetic for arbitrary parameters. Input arrays remain unchanged; callback exceptions/side effects/concurrent safety belong to caller.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ struct Zero final:dm::fem::ScalarField1D{double evaluate(double) override{return 0;}} source;
⍝ const auto t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{},{0,1,0},.5,.5);
⍝ std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2 0.142857
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - Arnold (2012), Numerical Analysis of Partial Differential Equations, chapter5 section2.
⍝   https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~arnold/8445.f12/notes.pdf . Native load quadrature,
⍝   fixed data and rounded/shortened time grid are implementation choices.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve_transient mesh p q f left right u0 t_end dt
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `mesh` Mesh1D handle: Borrowed valid mesh with at least two finite increasing nodes.
⍝ - `p` numeric vector: Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
⍝ - `q` numeric vector: Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
⍝ - `f` ScalarField1D handle: Borrowed spatial callback, reevaluated at every advance.
⍝ - `left` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Fixed left condition, with outward normal -1.
⍝ - `right` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Fixed right condition, with outward normal +1.
⍝ - `u0` numeric vector: Borrowed finite initial nodal values, exactly one per mesh node.
⍝ - `t_end` number: Positive finite final time, in time units.
⍝ - `dt` number: Positive finite nominal time step in the same units; may exceed t_end.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** FEM1DTimeSeries handle: Owned nodes, initial state and strictly advancing slices ending at t_end.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: For fewer than two nodes, wrong coefficient/u0 lengths or nonpositive/nonfinite time controls. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: If frame counts, vector capacities or total scalar count cannot be represented. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: arithmetic_error: …`: If rounded time products cannot advance before t_end. (C++ `std::overflow_error`)
⍝ - WS FULL `dm: allocation: …`: If output/assembly storage cannot be allocated; callback exceptions propagate. (C++ `std::bad_alloc`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `FEM1DTimeSeries datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const std::vector<double> & q, ScalarField1D & f, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right, const std::vector<double> & u0, double t_end, double dt)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆solve_transient_builtin()`, `dm∆FEM1DTimeSeries`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(667 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve_transient_builtin B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Integrate the same backward-Euler model with a named source and no callback subclass. Uses the same private source construction as solve_builtin() and the same actual time loop as solve_transient(); no second solver or per-language glue. Names/defaults: zero=0; constant=c ({1}); linear=m*x+c ({1,0}); polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty0); sine=A*sin(w*x+phase) ({1,1,0}). Extra entries ignored except polynomial; exact case-sensitive names. Source objects are local and synchronous; results own values, not callback aliases. All spatial/time/initial-state, complexity and stability contracts follow solve_transient(); ordinary output has no optional history/quota.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{},{0,0,0},.5,.5);
⍝ std::print("{} {:.6f}\n",t.num_steps(),t.value_at(1,1)); // 2 0.107143
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~arnold/8445.f12/notes.pdf ; same native discretization as solve_transient().
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆FEM1D∆solve_transient_builtin mesh p q source source_params left right u0 t_end dt
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `mesh` Mesh1D handle: Borrowed valid finite increasing mesh, with at least two nodes.
⍝ - `p` numeric vector: Borrowed scalar/per-element diffusion coefficient.
⍝ - `q` numeric vector: Borrowed scalar/per-element reaction coefficient.
⍝ - `source` character vector: Exact name zero, constant, linear, polynomial or sine.
⍝ - `source_params` numeric vector: Borrowed positional parameters; omitted trailing values use the defaults above.
⍝ - `left` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Fixed left boundary condition using outward normal -1.
⍝ - `right` BoundaryCondition1D handle: Fixed right boundary condition using outward normal +1.
⍝ - `u0` numeric vector: Borrowed finite initial values, exactly one per spatial node.
⍝ - `t_end` number: Positive finite final time.
⍝ - `dt` number: Positive finite nominal time step; final interval is shortened as needed.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** FEM1DTimeSeries handle: Owned initial state and actual strictly advancing backward-Euler slices.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: For an unknown source, malformed coefficient/u0 lengths, fewer than two nodes or nonpositive/nonfinite time controls. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: If frame/container/total scalar counts cannot be represented. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: arithmetic_error: …`: If rounded time products cannot advance. (C++ `std::overflow_error`)
⍝ - WS FULL `dm: allocation: …`: If parameters, output or assembly storage cannot be allocated. (C++ `std::bad_alloc`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `FEM1DTimeSeries datamunge::fem::FEM1D::solve_transient_builtin(const Mesh1D & mesh, const std::vector<double> & p, const std::vector<double> & q, const std::string & source, const std::vector<double> & source_params, const BoundaryCondition1D & left, const BoundaryCondition1D & right, const std::vector<double> & u0, double t_end, double dt)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆solve_builtin()`, `dm∆solve_transient()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(668 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
