∇Z←dm∆DelaunayWork∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Actual seed and cavity operations, excluding validation, sorting and copies. A conflict test is either an incircle test on a finite face or an exact half-plane test on a ghost. Counters exclude CCW checks on newly created faces, between-endpoint comparisons, map operations, allocation, trace copies and final sorting. Initial seed plus three ghosts are excluded from creation/removal counts. No counts are estimates of time or fixed-predicate internal arithmetic.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{4,0},{4,4},{0,4},{2,2}});
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n",t.work.insertions,t.work.incircle_tests+t.work.hull_side_tests); // 2 10
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆DelaunayWork∆seed_orientation_tests` (field), `dm∆DelaunayWork∆insertions` (field), `dm∆DelaunayWork∆incircle_tests` (field), `dm∆DelaunayWork∆hull_side_tests` (field), `dm∆DelaunayWork∆removed_faces` (field), `dm∆DelaunayWork∆boundary_edges` (field), `dm∆DelaunayWork∆created_faces` (field).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('DelaunayWork' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆DelaunayWork∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** DelaunayWork handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::geometry::DelaunayWork::DelaunayWork()`
