∇Z←dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned actual cavity removal, directed boundary and replacement for one site. removed/added may contain ghosts, identified by c=the original input count. boundary is ordered by canonical undirected endpoint key but retains the first directed occurrence; shared interior edges are cancelled. Actual face scans precede this event. No full before/after mesh snapshot or geometric replay is retained. All vectors own their entries and have no input lifetime dependency.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{4,0},{4,4},{0,4},{2,2}});
⍝ std::print("{} {} {}\n",t.steps.back().input_index,t.steps.back().removed.size(),t.steps.back().added.size()); // 4 2 4
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆input_index` (field), `dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆faces_before` (field), `dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆faces_after` (field), `dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆removed` (field), `dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆boundary` (field), `dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆added` (field).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('DelaunayInsertion' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆DelaunayInsertion∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** DelaunayInsertion handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::geometry::DelaunayInsertion::DelaunayInsertion()`
