∇Z←dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The constant-gain alpha-beta ("g-h") filter: a constant-velocity tracker that uses the SAME predict/correct structure as KalmanFilter, but with fixed gains alpha (position correction) and beta (velocity correction) instead of a covariance-driven Kalman gain -- it is exactly the steady-state behavior a 1D constant-velocity KalmanFilter converges to once its covariance stops changing, with the covariance bookkeeping stripped out entirely. Far cheaper per step (no matrices at all) at the cost of not adapting its gain to changing noise conditions the way a real Kalman filter does.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆update`, `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆position`, `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆velocity`, `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆alpha`, `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆beta`, `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆dt`, `dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆filter`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('AlphaBetaFilter' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆new alpha beta dt
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆new alpha beta dt x0
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆new alpha beta dt x0 v0
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `alpha` number
⍝ - `beta` number
⍝ - `dt` number
⍝ - `x0` number, default 0.0
⍝ - `v0` number, default 0.0
⍝
⍝ **Result:** AlphaBetaFilter handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaFilter::AlphaBetaFilter(double alpha, double beta, double dt, double x0 = 0.0, double v0 = 0.0)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 770) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆update B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Predicts one step ahead, then corrects toward measurement `z`: x_pred = x + v*dt; residual = z - x_pred; x = x_pred + alpha*residual; v += (beta/dt)*residual.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆AlphaBetaFilter∆update z
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `z` number
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaFilter::update(double z)`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(763 0 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
