∇Z←dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The constant-gain alpha-beta-gamma filter: AlphaBetaFilter's constant-ACCELERATION generalization (a 3-state g-h-k filter), adding a third fixed gain gamma for the acceleration correction. Same fixed-gain-vs-adaptive-Kalman-gain tradeoff as AlphaBetaFilter, one derivative order higher.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆update`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆position`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆velocity`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆acceleration`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆alpha`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆beta`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆gamma`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆dt`, `dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆filter`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('AlphaBetaGammaFilter' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆new alpha beta gamma dt
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆new alpha beta gamma dt x0
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆new alpha beta gamma dt x0 v0
⍝ obj←dm∆AlphaBetaGammaFilter∆new alpha beta gamma dt x0 v0 a0
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `alpha` number
⍝ - `beta` number
⍝ - `gamma` number
⍝ - `dt` number
⍝ - `x0` number, default 0.0
⍝ - `v0` number, default 0.0
⍝ - `a0` number, default 0.0
⍝
⍝ **Result:** AlphaBetaGammaFilter handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::filter::AlphaBetaGammaFilter::AlphaBetaGammaFilter(double alpha, double beta, double gamma, double dt, double x0 = 0.0, double v0 = 0.0, double a0 = 0.0)`
