∇Z←dm∆KalmanFilter∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The standard discrete-time linear Kalman filter: x_k = F x_{k-1} + w_k, z_k = H x_k + v_k, w_k ~ N(0, Q), v_k ~ N(0, R) -- the minimum-mean-squared-error linear   estimator for exactly this model. Stateful: holds the current (x, P) estimate,   mutated in place by predict()/update(); F, H, Q, R are fixed for the filter's   lifetime (construct a new filter if they change over time).
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆KalmanFilter∆predict`, `dm∆KalmanFilter∆update`, `dm∆KalmanFilter∆state`, `dm∆KalmanFilter∆covariance`, `dm∆KalmanFilter∆filter`, `dm∆KalmanFilter∆smooth`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('KalmanFilter' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆KalmanFilter∆new F H_ Q R x0 P0
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `F` numeric matrix (one row per element)
⍝ - `H_` numeric matrix (one row per element)
⍝ - `Q` numeric matrix (one row per element)
⍝ - `R` numeric matrix (one row per element)
⍝ - `x0` numeric vector
⍝ - `P0` numeric matrix (one row per element)
⍝
⍝ **Result:** KalmanFilter handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::filter::KalmanFilter::KalmanFilter(std::vector<std::vector<double>> F, std::vector<std::vector<double>> H, std::vector<std::vector<double>> Q, std::vector<std::vector<double>> R, std::vector<double> x0, std::vector<std::vector<double>> P0)`
