∇H dm∆KalmanFilter∆update B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ The measurement-update (correction) step given observation `z`: the standard innovation-covariance / Kalman-gain form (S = H P H^T + R, K = P H^T S^-1, x += K(z - Hx), P = (I - KH) P) -- not the numerically-hardened Joseph form, matching this codebase's general preference for the textbook formula over a more robust but more complex alternative.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆KalmanFilter∆update z
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `z` numeric vector
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::filter::KalmanFilter::update(const std::vector<double> & z)`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(799 0 H) dm⍙native B
