∇Z←dm∆ConvexHullWork∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Actual sorting, deduplication and two-scan work, with checked counters. Comparison counts depend on the standard-library sort and original order. For at least two distinct points each pass pushes each point once. Tests count exact orientation requests; every nonpositive test causes one pop. max_stack is the greatest length of either separate chain, not their sum.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{0,0},{1,0},{0,1}});
⍝ std::cout << a.work.distinct_points << ' ' << a.work.pushes; // 3 6
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆input_points` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆distinct_points` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆sort_comparisons` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆duplicate_comparisons` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆orientation_tests` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆pushes` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆pops` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullWork∆max_stack` (field).
⍝
