∇Z←dm∆ConvexHullAnalysis∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned strict hull, earliest original identities and actual work without history. Vertices start at the lexicographic minimum and run counterclockwise, without repeating the first. Collinear edge points are omitted. Empty gives no points; one distinct point gives one; a collinear set gives its sorted two endpoints. Identity vector aligns one-for-one with hull vertices.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{1,0},{0,0},{0,1}});
⍝ std::cout << a.hull.size() << ' ' << a.input_indices[0]; // 3 1
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ConvexHullAnalysis∆hull` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullAnalysis∆input_indices` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullAnalysis∆work` (field).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ConvexHullAnalysis' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ConvexHullAnalysis∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ConvexHullAnalysis handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::geometry::ConvexHullAnalysis::ConvexHullAnalysis()`
