∇Z←dm∆ConvexHullTrace∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned actual sorted identities, compact stack edits and completed scan chains. lower/upper contain indices into sorted and include their endpoints. Inputs with fewer than two distinct points take no scans and have empty chains/events. Trace capture performs no extra sorting or orientation replay. All storage is independent of the caller, result and other snapshots; O(n) extra space.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::geometry::convex_hull_trace({{0,0},{1,0}});
⍝ std::cout << t.lower.size() << ' ' << t.upper.size(); // 2 2
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ConvexHullTrace∆analysis` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullTrace∆sorted` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullTrace∆events` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullTrace∆lower` (field), `dm∆ConvexHullTrace∆upper` (field).
