∇Z←P dm∆Callback∆subclass B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ An APL implementation of `dm∆Callback`: C++ calls the APL functions Impl∆method for its virtual methods.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←'Impl' dm∆Callback∆subclass
⍝ ```
⍝ `Impl` is a name prefix: for each overridable method below, a defined function `Impl∆method` overrides it,
⍝ called as `Z←obj Impl∆method args` (`Z←Impl∆method obj` without arguments, the same conventions as the
⍝ generated functions). Methods without an APL function run the C++ implementation.
⍝
⍝ **Overridable:**
⍝ - `call` — C++ `double datamunge::Callback::call(double x)`
⍝
⍝ The object lives until `dm∆Delete obj`, or while C++ owns it.
