∇Z←H dm∆Plot∆margins B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Overrides the automatic outer margins (in pixels) around the plotting area, e.g. for small multi-panel tiles. The defaults leave room for a title, axis labels, and ticks; tight margins suit panels whose title and axis labels are empty.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆Plot∆margins left right top bottom
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `left` number: Left margin in pixels (default 90).
⍝ - `right` number: Right margin in pixels (default 24).
⍝ - `top` number: Top margin in pixels (default 72, plus 24 when a subtitle is set).
⍝ - `bottom` number: Bottom margin in pixels (default 84).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Plot handle: This plot, for chaining.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If any margin is negative or non-finite. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `Plot & datamunge::graphics::Plot::margins(double left, double right, double top, double bottom)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆margins()`
