 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆Plot∆show B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Opens the plot in an interactive X11 window and blocks until it is closed (like printing a plot in an interactive R session).
⍝
⍝ The window has toolbar and keyboard zoom/pan (it re-renders from data bounds) and closes
⍝ on q or Escape; the function returns only then. The window title is `title_hint`, or
⍝ the plot's title (title_text()) when the hint is empty. Requires a build with X11 support and a reachable `DISPLAY`; use save()
⍝ in headless code such as tests and CI.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto x = dm::runif(0, 1, 1000);
⍝ const auto y = dm::sin(20 / (x + 0.25)) + dm::rnorm(0, 0.2, 1000);
⍝ dm::Plot(x, y).set_title("Doppler").set_col("blue").show("Doppler signal");
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆Plot∆show ⍬
⍝ obj dm∆Plot∆show title_hint
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `title_hint` character vector, default '': Window title; empty (the default) uses the plot's title.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If X11 support was not compiled in, the display cannot be opened, its visual is unsupported, or the plot has no data series. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::graphics::Plot::show(const std::string & title_hint = "") const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆save()`, `dm∆to_svg()`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(1017 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆RPlot∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A single R-base-graphics-style plot, spelled `dm::Plot` in user code.
⍝
⍝ Covers R's high-level plotting calls (`plot()`, `hist()`, `barplot()`, `boxplot()`, `pie()`,
⍝ `curve()`, `qqnorm()`, ...) as constructors and static factories, plus the "add to the
⍝ current plot" verbs R exposes as separate functions (`points()`, `lines()`, `abline()`,
⍝ `legend()`, `text()`, ...) as chainable member functions. A plot is an ordinary value: it
⍝ owns copies of its data, copies cheaply enough to pass around, and draws nothing until it
⍝ is rendered with to_svg(), save(), or show().
⍝
⍝ Two composition styles mix freely. Setters such as set_title() and verbs such as points()
⍝ mutate the plot and return `RPlot&` for chaining; the pipe `plot | dm::points(...)` (see
⍝ compose.hpp) appends a reusable layer to a copy. A fresh plot has the title
⍝ "datamunge plot", axis labels "x" and "y", a 960x640 canvas, and a light grid.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto x = dm::seql(-2.0, 2.0, 9);
⍝ auto plt = dm::Plot(x, x * x)
⍝                .set_title("Parabola")
⍝                .set_xlab("x")
⍝                .set_ylab("x squared");
⍝ plt.lines(x, x * x, dm::RGB{220, 38, 38}).abline_h(0.0);
⍝ plt.save("parabola.svg");
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ Derives from `dm∆Plot`: their functions accept RPlot handles.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆RPlot∆create` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆size`, `dm∆RPlot∆title`, `dm∆RPlot∆subtitle`, `dm∆RPlot∆x_label`, `dm∆RPlot∆y_label`, `dm∆RPlot∆xlab`, `dm∆RPlot∆ylab`, `dm∆RPlot∆set_title`, `dm∆RPlot∆set_subtitle`, `dm∆RPlot∆set_xlab`, `dm∆RPlot∆set_ylab`, `dm∆RPlot∆set_col`, `dm∆RPlot∆background`, `dm∆RPlot∆axis_color`, `dm∆RPlot∆grid_color`, `dm∆RPlot∆show_grid`, `dm∆RPlot∆x_limits`, `dm∆RPlot∆y_limits`, `dm∆RPlot∆xlim`, `dm∆RPlot∆ylim`, `dm∆RPlot∆hide_axes`, `dm∆RPlot∆x_tick_labels`, `dm∆RPlot∆x_ticks`, `dm∆RPlot∆y_tick_labels`, `dm∆RPlot∆y_ticks`, `dm∆RPlot∆margins`, `dm∆RPlot∆tick_font_size`, `dm∆RPlot∆pretty_ticks`, `dm∆RPlot∆plot` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆hist` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆barplot` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆boxplot` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆pie` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆curve` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆qqnorm` (static), `dm∆RPlot∆points`, `dm∆RPlot∆points_colored`, `dm∆RPlot∆line`, `dm∆RPlot∆lines`, `dm∆RPlot∆bars`, `dm∆RPlot∆box`, `dm∆RPlot∆abline`, `dm∆RPlot∆abline_h`, `dm∆RPlot∆abline_v`, `dm∆RPlot∆qqline`, `dm∆RPlot∆legend`, `dm∆RPlot∆text`, `dm∆RPlot∆polygon`, `dm∆RPlot∆image`, `dm∆RPlot∆segments`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('RPlot' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆RPlot∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆RPlot∆new x y
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Constructs an empty plot with default labels and styling, ready for layers.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** RPlot handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::graphics::RPlot::RPlot()`
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::graphics::RPlot::RPlot(std::vector<double> x, std::vector<double> y)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1070) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
