∇Z←dm∆RPlot∆barplot B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Builds a bar chart with one bar per height, like R's `barplot(heights, names.arg = names)`.
⍝
⍝ Bar i is centered at x = i (0, 1, 2, ...) and is 0.8 units wide (R puts default bars at
⍝ 0.7, 1.9, 3.1, ...). Bars rise from 0, so negative heights point down, and the y range
⍝ always includes 0. Nonempty `names` become x tick labels under the bars. The title and
⍝ axis labels keep their defaults.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto plt = dm::Plot::barplot({3.0, 5.0, 2.0}, {"a", "b", "c"}).set_title("Counts");
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n", plt.series()[0].x[2], plt.x_tick_label_list()[2]);  // 2 c
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - R `barplot()`: https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/barplot.html
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆RPlot∆barplot heights
⍝ Z←dm∆RPlot∆barplot heights names
⍝ Z←dm∆RPlot∆barplot heights names label
⍝ Z←dm∆RPlot∆barplot heights names label color
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `heights` numeric vector: Bar heights, in display order.
⍝ - `names` vector of character vectors, default the C++ default: Tick labels, one per bar; empty (the default) keeps numeric ticks.
⍝ - `label` character vector, default '': Legend text; empty (the default) shows no legend.
⍝ - `color` RGB handle, default the C++ default: Bar color (default green `{22, 163, 74}`).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** RPlot handle: A new plot holding one Bar series.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If `heights` is empty or `names` is nonempty with a different length. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `RPlot datamunge::graphics::RPlot::barplot(std::vector<double> heights, std::vector<std::string> names = {}, std::string label = "", RGBA color = ...)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆bars()`, `dm∆x_tick_labels()`
