∇Z←H dm∆RPlot∆points_colored B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Appends scatter points with a recycled per-point RGB(A) palette. Coordinates must have equal nonzero lengths; colors must not be empty. A partial palette cycle is allowed without a warning. Colors retain their own alpha. The series is unlabeled, so it never appears in the automatic legend.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto palette = dm::c(dm::RGB{255, 0, 0}, dm::RGB{0, 0, 255});
⍝ auto plt = dm::Plot().points_colored(dm::c(1.0, 2.0, 3.0), dm::c(3.0, 2.0, 1.0), palette);
⍝ std::print("{}\n", plt.series()[0].point_colors.size());  // 2 (red, blue, red)
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - R `points()` (vector `col`): https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/points.html
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆RPlot∆points_colored x y colors
⍝ Z←obj dm∆RPlot∆points_colored x y colors marker_size
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `x` numeric vector: Horizontal coordinates.
⍝ - `y` numeric vector: Vertical coordinates, paired with `x`.
⍝ - `colors` vector of (RGB handle): Palette; point i uses `colors[i % colors.size()]`.
⍝ - `marker_size` number, default 4.0: Marker radius in pixels (default 4).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** RPlot handle: This plot, for chaining.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If the coordinate lengths or palette are invalid. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `RPlot & datamunge::graphics::RPlot::points_colored(std::vector<double> x, std::vector<double> y, std::vector<RGBA> colors, double marker_size = 4.0)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆set_col()`, `dm∆the pipe-friendly form of this call.`
