∇Z←H dm∆RPlot∆abline_v B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Adds a vertical reference line at x = `x_value`, like R's `abline(v = x_value)`.
⍝
⍝ Spans the full height of the plotting area beneath the data. Unlike horizontal and
⍝ sloped lines, it widens the automatic x range to include `x_value`.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ See abline().
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - R `abline()`: https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/graphics/html/abline.html
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆RPlot∆abline_v x_value
⍝ Z←obj dm∆RPlot∆abline_v x_value color
⍝ Z←obj dm∆RPlot∆abline_v x_value color stroke_width
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `x_value` number: Horizontal position of the line, in data units.
⍝ - `color` RGB handle, default the C++ default: Line color (default opaque black).
⍝ - `stroke_width` number, default 1.0: Line width in pixels (default 1).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** RPlot handle: This plot, for chaining.
⍝
⍝ - **Warning:** Only to_svg() and `.svg` saves draw reference lines. The raster outputs (`.png`, `.pdf`, and show()) currently omit them.
⍝
⍝ - C++: `RPlot & datamunge::graphics::RPlot::abline_v(double x_value, RGBA color = ..., double stroke_width = 1.0)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆abline()`, `dm∆abline_h()`
