 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆RLayout∆fit_panels H;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Resizes every stored panel's canvas to its cell, so text keeps its pixel size instead of being scaled with the panel.
⍝
⍝ Call it after size() and title() (the title band changes the cell height). Panels added
⍝ later keep their own size until fit_panels() is called again. A cell whose shorter side is
⍝ under min_panel_px gets a canvas scaled up to that side (same aspect ratio), so its text is
⍝ drawn proportionally smaller instead of the margins overflowing the panel.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
⍝                .add(dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(2.0, 1.0)))
⍝                .add(dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0), dm::c(1.0, 2.0)))
⍝                .size(1000, 400)
⍝                .fit_panels();
⍝ std::print("{}x{}\n", fig.panel(0).width(), fig.panel(0).height());  // 500x400
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆RLayout∆fit_panels obj
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** RLayout handle: This layout, for chaining.
⍝
⍝ - C++: `RLayout & datamunge::graphics::RLayout::fit_panels()`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆size()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1089 2 H) dm⍙native ⍬
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆RLayout∆show B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Opens the tiled figure in the interactive X11 viewer; the toolbar zoom/pan buttons act on every panel's data bounds at once, keyboard zoom/pan scales the whole image.
⍝
⍝ Blocks until the window is closed (q or Escape). Use save() in headless code.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto x = dm::seql(0.0, 6.0, 30);
⍝ dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
⍝     .add(dm::Plot(x, dm::sin(x)))
⍝     .add(dm::Plot(x, dm::cos(x)))
⍝     .show("Trig");
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆RLayout∆show ⍬
⍝ obj dm∆RLayout∆show title_hint
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `title_hint` character vector, default '': Window title; empty (the default) uses title_text().
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If X11 support was not enabled at build time or no display is available. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If no panel was added. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::graphics::RLayout::show(const std::string & title_hint = "") const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆save()`, `dm∆show()`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(1090 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

