∇Z←dm∆DTWResult∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned unrestricted scalar DTW result, preserving the original three-field layout. Distance is the unnormalized sum of absolute differences along the returned inclusive path. Default construction is an uncomputed placeholder. Copies own independent buffers. Positive lengths fit int; steps advance a, b or both by one.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto r=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping({1,2,3},{1,1,2,3});
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n",r.distance,r.path_a.size()); // 0 4
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆DTWResult∆distance` (field), `dm∆DTWResult∆path_a` (field), `dm∆DTWResult∆path_b` (field).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('DTWResult' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆DTWResult∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** DTWResult handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::geometry::DTWResult::DTWResult()`
