∇Z←dm∆DTWTrace∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned input, actual accumulated costs and chosen predecessors from one DTW run. Positive cells are row-major at i*b.size()+j; sentinel border is implicit. Costs and predecessor codes are captured during the original recurrence, not reconstructed afterward. Infinite cells mark unrepresentable costs. Logical capture entries are a.size()+b.size()+2*a.size()*b.size(): one per input scalar, cost and direction. Result paths, rolling scratch rows, scalar metadata and allocator bytes are excluded. Copies are independent.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1},{4});
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n",t.cumulative[0],t.captured_entries); // 3 4
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆DTWTrace∆a` (field), `dm∆DTWTrace∆b` (field), `dm∆DTWTrace∆cumulative` (field), `dm∆DTWTrace∆predecessors` (field), `dm∆DTWTrace∆result` (field), `dm∆DTWTrace∆work` (field), `dm∆DTWTrace∆captured_entries` (field).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('DTWTrace' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆DTWTrace∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** DTWTrace handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::geometry::DTWTrace::DTWTrace()`
