⍝ One numerically integrated trajectory: t[i] paired with y[i] (the full state vector at that time), in increasing-time order, always including both endpoints. `t` and `y` are public fields for direct C++ use, but are not exposed to language bindings (a container-typed struct *field getter* -- even a plain vector<double>, not just a nested vector<vector<double>> -- hits a swig-jse R-backend codegen bug that a same-shaped plain *method* return does not) -- time_at()/state_at()/size() are the cross-language-safe way to read it.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ODESolution∆steps_taken` (field), `dm∆ODESolution∆function_evaluations` (field), `dm∆ODESolution∆size`, `dm∆ODESolution∆time_at`, `dm∆ODESolution∆state_at`.
