∇Z←dm∆AdaDelta∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ AdaDelta on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface. Uses squared-gradient and squared-update exponential averages. The update multiplies the gradient by sqrt(previous_update_average+epsilon)/sqrt(current_gradient_average+epsilon). No separate learning-rate option. Tests the gradient used after applying its update; O(p) reset local state. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const dm::optim::AdaDelta optimizer;
⍝ std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 10000
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - M. D. Zeiler (2012), ADADELTA: An Adaptive Learning Rate Method, https://arxiv.org/abs/1212.5701
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆AdaDelta∆optimize`, `dm∆AdaDelta∆options`.
⍝
