∇Z←H dm∆AdaDelta∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Run AdaDelta from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Uses squared-gradient and squared-update exponential averages. The update multiplies the gradient by sqrt(previous_update_average+epsilon)/sqrt(current_gradient_average+epsilon). No separate learning-rate option. Tests the gradient used after applying its update; O(p) reset local state.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
⍝ dm::optim::AdaDeltaOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
⍝ std::vector<double> x{0,0};
⍝ const auto value=dm::optim::AdaDelta(controls).optimize(f,x);
⍝ std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆AdaDelta∆optimize function coordinates
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` DifferentiableFunction handle: Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite output shapes.
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z): Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector): Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: AdaDelta: decay_rate must be in [0, 1); AdaDelta: epsilon must be positive; AdaDelta: tolerance must be non-negative. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs. (C++ `std::exception`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::AdaDelta::optimize(DifferentiableFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆trace_optimize()`, `dm∆AdaDeltaOptions`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1254 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
