∇Z←dm∆ArtificialBeeColony∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Artificial Bee Colony (Karaboga, 2005): a swarm-intelligence method inspired by honey bee foraging. Employed bees exploit known food sources, onlooker bees probabilistically favor the fitter sources, and scout bees replace sources that have stagnated for too long. Derivative-free, box-constrained.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ArtificialBeeColony∆optimize`, `dm∆ArtificialBeeColony∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ArtificialBeeColony' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ArtificialBeeColony∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆ArtificialBeeColony∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
