∇Z←H dm∆BayesianOptimization∆run B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Runs the loop and records every evaluation.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆BayesianOptimization∆run function lower upper surrogate
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle: Objective to minimise.
⍝ - `lower` numeric vector: Lower corner of the box.
⍝ - `upper` numeric vector: Upper corner of the box (each entry larger than in `lower`).
⍝ - `surrogate` BayesianSurrogate handle: Surrogate refitted before every proposal.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** BayesianOptimizationResult handle: The evaluations and the best point.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If the bounds are empty, differ in length or are not increasing. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `BayesianOptimizationResult datamunge::optim::BayesianOptimization::run(ArbitraryFunction & function, const std::vector<double> & lower, const std::vector<double> & upper, BayesianSurrogate & surrogate) const`
