 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆BayesianOptimization∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Runs the loop and returns only the best value.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆BayesianOptimization∆optimize function coordinates lower upper surrogate
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle: Objective to minimise.
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z): Output: the best point (its length must equal the bounds').
⍝ - `lower` numeric vector: Lower corner of the box.
⍝ - `upper` numeric vector: Upper corner of the box.
⍝ - `surrogate` BayesianSurrogate handle: Surrogate refitted before every proposal.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector): The smallest observed value.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If the bounds do not match `coordinates` or are not increasing. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::BayesianOptimization::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double> & lower, const std::vector<double> & upper, BayesianSurrogate & surrogate) const`
