∇

∇Z←H dm∆CoordinateDescent∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Run CoordinateDescent from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Each epoch visits coordinates in index order. Every partial update requests a full gradient and an Armijo-backtracked value sequence; this is not exact one-dimensional minimisation. An exhausted search restores that coordinate. Stops on the full end-of-epoch gradient norm.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
⍝ dm::optim::CoordinateDescentOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
⍝ std::vector<double> x{0,0};
⍝ const auto value=dm::optim::CoordinateDescent(controls).optimize(f,x);
⍝ std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆CoordinateDescent∆optimize function coordinates
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` DifferentiableFunction handle: Borrowed DifferentiableFunction with matching finite output shapes.
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z): Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector): Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: CoordinateDescent: step_size must be positive; CoordinateDescent: tolerance must be non-negative; CoordinateDescent: armijo_c1 must be in (0, 1); CoordinateDescent: backtracking_factor must be in (0, 1). (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs. (C++ `std::exception`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::CoordinateDescent::optimize(DifferentiableFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆trace_optimize()`, `dm∆CoordinateDescentOptions`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1373 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
