∇Z←dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The Cross-Entropy Method (CEM) for derivative-free continuous optimization on an ArbitraryFunction within a box constraint. A diagonal-covariance Gaussian search distribution is repeatedly refit from the best ("elite") fraction of each generation's samples, with the new distribution parameters exponentially smoothed against the previous generation's for stability (Rubinstein 1997; Rubinstein & Kroese 2004).
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆optimize`, `dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('CrossEntropyMethod' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` CrossEntropyMethodOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** CrossEntropyMethod handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::CrossEntropyMethod::CrossEntropyMethod(CrossEntropyMethodOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1393) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`], updating `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns its value. The initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed the initial distribution mean.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆CrossEntropyMethod∆optimize function coordinates lower_bound upper_bound
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z)
⍝ - `lower_bound` numeric vector
⍝ - `upper_bound` numeric vector
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::CrossEntropyMethod::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound) const`
