∇Z←dm∆CuckooSearchOptions∆discovery_rate H;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ pa: fraction of the worst nests discovered/abandoned each iteration. Yang & Deb's original paper headlines 0.25, but this implementation's "replace a randomly chosen comparison nest" Levy-flight rule (faithful to the paper) homogenizes the population fast enough at pa=0.25 that convergence quality becomes sharply seed-dependent on smooth objectives (verified: only 6/30 seeds converged well at pa=0.25, population_size=25 on a simple 3D sphere). 0.4 -- still within the commonly-used literature range -- injects enough fresh diversity each iteration to fix this at the default population size (verified: 30/30 seeds).
⍝
⍝ **Usage:** `Z←dm∆CuckooSearchOptions∆discovery_rate obj`; set it with `obj dm∆CuckooSearchOptions∆discovery_rate∆set value`
⍝
⍝ **Result:** number
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::CuckooSearchOptions::discovery_rate`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1396 2 H) dm⍙native ⍬
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

