∇Z←dm∆CuckooSearch∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Cuckoo Search (Yang & Deb, 2009) on an ArbitraryFunction within a box constraint: a population of nests is perturbed by heavy-tailed Levy flights (via Mantegna's algorithm) and a fraction of the worst nests is abandoned and rebuilt each iteration, mimicking brood parasitism. Derivative-free.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆CuckooSearch∆optimize`, `dm∆CuckooSearch∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('CuckooSearch' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆CuckooSearch∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆CuckooSearch∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` CuckooSearchOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** CuckooSearch handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::CuckooSearch::CuckooSearch(CuckooSearchOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1411) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆CuckooSearch∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`], updating `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns its value. The initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed one nest of the population.
