∇Z←dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ DifferentialEvolution on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface. Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
⍝ std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - R. Storn and K. Price (1997), Differential Evolution - A Simple and Efficient Heuristic for global Optimization over Continuous Spaces, https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1008202821328
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆optimize`, `dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('DifferentialEvolution' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` DEOptions handle, default the C++ default: Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by DEOptions.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** DifferentialEvolution handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::DifferentialEvolution(DEOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1431) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Run DifferentialEvolution from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
⍝ dm::optim::DEOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
⍝ std::vector<double> x{0,0};
⍝ const auto value=dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆DifferentialEvolution∆optimize function coordinates lower_bound upper_bound
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle: Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z): Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.
⍝ - `lower_bound` numeric vector: Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.
⍝ - `upper_bound` numeric vector: Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than lower limits.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector): Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: DifferentialEvolution::optimize: crossover_strategy must be 'binomial' or 'exponential'. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs. (C++ `std::exception`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound) const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆trace_optimize()`, `dm∆DEOptions`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1429 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

