∇Z←dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The Firefly Algorithm (Yang, 2008/2009): a population of fireflies is pairwise attracted toward brighter (better) neighbors, with attractiveness decaying with squared distance and a shrinking random-walk term for exploration. Derivative-free, O(n^2) per iteration in the population size.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆optimize`, `dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('FireflyAlgorithm' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` FireflyAlgorithmOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** FireflyAlgorithm handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm::FireflyAlgorithm(FireflyAlgorithmOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1487) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`], updating `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns its value. The initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed one member of the population.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆FireflyAlgorithm∆optimize function coordinates lower_bound upper_bound
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z)
⍝ - `lower_bound` numeric vector
⍝ - `upper_bound` numeric vector
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound) const`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1485 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
