∇Z←dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ GeneticAlgorithm on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface. Real-valued box-constrained selection, crossover, Gaussian mutation and optional elitism. Initial coordinates seed a clamped population member. Returns the best visited point and can stop after more than twenty small-best-improvement generations. O(population_size*p) storage; strategy/rate choices affect results, with no global certificate. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const dm::optim::GeneticAlgorithm optimizer;
⍝ std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - J. H. Holland (1992 reprint), Adaptation in Natural and Artificial Systems, MIT Press, https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262581110/adaptation-in-natural-and-artificial-systems/. This implementation uses real-valued operators, as specified above, rather than binary chromosomes.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆optimize`, `dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('GeneticAlgorithm' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` GAOptions handle, default the C++ default: Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by GAOptions.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** GeneticAlgorithm handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::GeneticAlgorithm::GeneticAlgorithm(GAOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1527) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Run GeneticAlgorithm from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Real-valued box-constrained selection, crossover, Gaussian mutation and optional elitism. Initial coordinates seed a clamped population member. Returns the best visited point and can stop after more than twenty small-best-improvement generations. O(population_size*p) storage; strategy/rate choices affect results, with no global certificate.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
⍝ dm::optim::GAOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
⍝ std::vector<double> x{0,0};
⍝ const auto value=dm::optim::GeneticAlgorithm(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆GeneticAlgorithm∆optimize function coordinates lower_bound upper_bound
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle: Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z): Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.
⍝ - `lower_bound` numeric vector: Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.
⍝ - `upper_bound` numeric vector: Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than lower limits.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector): Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: GeneticAlgorithm::optimize: population_size must be at least 2. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs. (C++ `std::exception`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::GeneticAlgorithm::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound) const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆trace_optimize()`, `dm∆GAOptions`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1525 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

