∇Z←dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) on an ArbitraryFunction within a box constraint: a population of wolves is guided each iteration by its three best members (alpha, beta, delta), moving every wolf to the elementwise average of three independently randomized pulls toward those leaders. Derivative-free. Mirjalili, Mirjalili & Lewis (2014), "Grey wolf optimizer", Advances in Engineering Software, 69, 46-61.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆optimize`, `dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('GreyWolfOptimizer' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` GreyWolfOptimizerOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** GreyWolfOptimizer handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::GreyWolfOptimizer::GreyWolfOptimizer(GreyWolfOptimizerOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1551) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Minimizes `function` within [`lower_bound`, `upper_bound`], updating `coordinates` in place to the best point found, and returns its value. The initial `coordinates` (clamped into bounds) seed one wolf of the population.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆GreyWolfOptimizer∆optimize function coordinates lower_bound upper_bound
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z)
⍝ - `lower_bound` numeric vector
⍝ - `upper_bound` numeric vector
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::GreyWolfOptimizer::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates, const std::vector<double> & lower_bound, const std::vector<double> & upper_bound) const`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1549 1 H) dm⍙native B
