∇Z←dm∆HarmonySearch∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Harmony search on an ArbitraryFunction within a box constraint: a fixed-size harmony memory of candidate solutions is improvised one new vector at a time, mixing memory consideration, pitch adjustment, and random selection per dimension, with greedy replacement of the worst memory member. Derivative-free.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆HarmonySearch∆optimize`, `dm∆HarmonySearch∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('HarmonySearch' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆HarmonySearch∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆HarmonySearch∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` HarmonySearchOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** HarmonySearch handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::HarmonySearch::HarmonySearch(HarmonySearchOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1569) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
