∇Z←dm∆ParallelTempering∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Parallel tempering (replica exchange Monte Carlo): the population-based generalization of SimulatedAnnealing. Runs num_replicas Metropolis chains simultaneously, each held at its own fixed temperature on a geometric ladder, and periodically proposes swapping adjacent-temperature replicas' states so hot chains help cold chains escape local minima. Derivative-free, unconstrained, suitable for non-differentiable/black-box objectives -- like SimulatedAnnealing, requires nothing beyond evaluate().
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ParallelTempering∆optimize`, `dm∆ParallelTempering∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ParallelTempering' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ParallelTempering∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆ParallelTempering∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` ParallelTemperingOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ParallelTempering handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::ParallelTempering::ParallelTempering(ParallelTemperingOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1683) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

