∇Z←dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Exact Gaussian-process regression surrogate with the squared-exponential kernel
⍝
⍝ `s\exp(-\lVert x-x'\rVert^2/2\ell^2)`.
⍝
⍝ fit() Cholesky-factors `K+\sigma_n^2I=LL^\top` once and solves for
⍝ `\alpha=(K+\sigma_n^2I)^{-1}(y-m)`; predict() then needs one forward substitution per point:
⍝ mean `m+k_*^\top\alpha` and variance `s-\lVert L^{-1}k_*\rVert^2`.
⍝
⍝ The two-argument constructor keeps the original fixed setup: zero prior mean, unit signal
⍝ variance, no normalisation or fitting, expected improvement. The options constructor adds
⍝ value normalisation, marginal-likelihood fitting of the hyperparameters and other acquisitions.
⍝ The kernel is isotropic, so the inputs should be on comparable scales.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::optim::RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate gp(1.0, 0.0);
⍝ gp.fit({{0.0}, {2.0}}, {1.0, -1.0});
⍝ const auto p = gp.predict({1.0});
⍝ std::print("{:.4f} {:.4f}\n", p.mean, p.sd);  // 0.0000 0.5933
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - C. E. Rasmussen and C. K. I. Williams (2006). *Gaussian Processes for Machine Learning*,
⍝   chapters 2 and 5. MIT Press.
⍝
⍝ Derives from `dm∆BayesianSurrogate`: their functions accept RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate handles.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆options`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆fit`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆acquisition`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆predict`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆log_marginal_likelihood`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆length_scale`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆noise`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆signal_variance`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆prior_mean`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆value_scale`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆points`, `dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆values`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆new length_scale
⍝ obj←dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆new length_scale noise
⍝ obj←dm∆RBFGaussianProcessSurrogate∆new options
⍝ ```
