∇Z←dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SimulatedAnnealing on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface. Gaussian random-walk proposals with geometrically decaying temperature and Metropolis acceptance of worse values. Returns the best visited point, not the last accepted state. A finite cooling schedule does not certify a global optimum; O(p) storage. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealing optimizer;
⍝ std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 10000
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - S. Kirkpatrick, C. D. Gelatt and M. P. Vecchi (1983), Optimization by Simulated Annealing, https://doi.org/10.1126/science.220.4598.671. Finite geometric cooling here supplies no global guarantee.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆optimize`, `dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆options`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('SimulatedAnnealing' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆new options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `options` SimulatedAnnealingOptions handle, default the C++ default: Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by SimulatedAnnealingOptions.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** SimulatedAnnealing handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::optim::SimulatedAnnealing::SimulatedAnnealing(SimulatedAnnealingOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1824) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←H dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆optimize B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Run SimulatedAnnealing from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Gaussian random-walk proposals with geometrically decaying temperature and Metropolis acceptance of worse values. Returns the best visited point, not the last accepted state. A finite cooling schedule does not certify a global optimum; O(p) storage.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
⍝ dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealingOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
⍝ std::vector<double> x{0,0};
⍝ const auto value=dm::optim::SimulatedAnnealing(controls).optimize(f,x);
⍝ std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆SimulatedAnnealing∆optimize function coordinates
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `function` ArbitraryFunction handle: Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.
⍝ - `coordinates` numeric vector (updated: returned in Z): Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** the result, then the updated arguments (one value alone, several as a vector): Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs. (C++ `std::exception`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::optim::SimulatedAnnealing::optimize(ArbitraryFunction & function, std::vector<double> & coordinates) const`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆trace_optimize()`, `dm∆SimulatedAnnealingOptions`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(1822 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

