∇Z←dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Owned hypothesis-test result, analogous to R's htest list. Each test documents which fields it populates and what its interval estimates. Unused numeric fields retain zero; this default is storage, not a claim of zero effect. Read bounds only when has_conf_int is true; one-sided intervals may be unbounded. p_value is a null-model tail probability, not a posterior probability of the null. Objects own their method string and contain no borrowed references or shared state.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::stats::t_test_one_sample({1,2,3,4});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",t.has_conf_int); // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/t.test.html
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆statistic` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆parameter1` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆parameter2` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆p_value` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆estimate1` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆estimate2` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆conf_int_lower` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆conf_int_upper` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆has_conf_int` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆alternative` (field), `dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆method` (field).
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('HypothesisTestResult' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆HypothesisTestResult∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** HypothesisTestResult handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::stats::HypothesisTestResult::HypothesisTestResult()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 2 1917) dm⍙native ⍬
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
