∇Z←dm∆ARIMA∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A Box-Jenkins seasonal ARIMA(p, d, q)(P, D, Q)_s model, fit to a single numeric series by conditional sum of squares (CSS): the series is differenced (regular d times, then seasonal D times with period s) to stationarity, the combined AR/MA polynomials (regular composed with seasonal, via polynomial multiplication) are estimated by minimizing the conditional residual sum of squares with DifferentialEvolution, and forecasts are produced by recursing the fitted difference equation forward and re-integrating through the differencing steps.
⍝
⍝ Setting seasonal_period == 0 (the default) reduces this to a plain, non-seasonal
⍝ ARIMA(p, d, q) model -- i.e. SARIMA is the general case, ARIMA the special case,
⍝ exactly as in R's arima()/statsmodels' SARIMAX().
⍝
⍝ Note: CSS estimation approximates the exact Gaussian likelihood by conditioning
⍝ on the first max(p + P*s, q + Q*s) observations rather than filtering the full
⍝ series (e.g. via a Kalman filter); it is a standard, textbook ARIMA fitting
⍝ method (R's arima(method = "CSS")) but will differ slightly from exact-ML fits.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ARIMA∆options`, `dm∆ARIMA∆ar_coefficients`, `dm∆ARIMA∆ma_coefficients`, `dm∆ARIMA∆seasonal_ar_coefficients`, `dm∆ARIMA∆seasonal_ma_coefficients`, `dm∆ARIMA∆mean`, `dm∆ARIMA∆observations`, `dm∆ARIMA∆n_used`, `dm∆ARIMA∆sigma2`, `dm∆ARIMA∆log_likelihood`, `dm∆ARIMA∆aic`, `dm∆ARIMA∆bic`, `dm∆ARIMA∆fitted_values`, `dm∆ARIMA∆residuals`, `dm∆ARIMA∆forecast`, `dm∆ARIMA∆expanded_ar_coefficients`, `dm∆ARIMA∆expanded_ma_coefficients`, `dm∆ARIMA∆psi_weights`, `dm∆ARIMA∆forecast_with_intervals`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ARIMA' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ARIMA∆new y
⍝ obj←dm∆ARIMA∆new y options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Fit the model to a series.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `y` numeric vector: The observed series, in time order.
⍝ - `options` ARIMAOptions handle, default the C++ default: Model orders and optimizer settings.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ARIMA handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If a seasonal order is set while seasonal_period is zero, or if the series is too short for the requested differencing or AR order. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::stats::ARIMA::ARIMA(const std::vector<double> & y, ARIMAOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 1962) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

