∇Z←dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Exponential smoothing (Holt-Winters family): simple exponential smoothing (no trend, no seasonality), Holt linear trend (with optional damping), and seasonal Holt-Winters (additive or multiplicative), unified under one class the way R's HoltWinters() and statsmodels' ExponentialSmoothing() are -- which components are active is controlled entirely by ExponentialSmoothingOptions::trend/seasonal.
⍝
⍝ Initial level/trend/seasonal-index states are set once from a simple classical
⍝ decomposition of the first one or two seasonal cycles and then held fixed; only
⍝ the smoothing parameters (alpha, beta, gamma, phi) are fit, by minimizing
⍝ one-step-ahead sum of squared errors with DifferentialEvolution.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆options`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆alpha`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆beta`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆gamma`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆phi`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆observations`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆sse`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆sigma2`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆log_likelihood`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆aic`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆bic`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆fitted_values`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆residuals`, `dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆forecast`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ExponentialSmoothing' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆new y
⍝ obj←dm∆ExponentialSmoothing∆new y options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `y` numeric vector
⍝ - `options` ExponentialSmoothingOptions handle, default the C++ default
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ExponentialSmoothing handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::stats::ExponentialSmoothing::ExponentialSmoothing(const std::vector<double> & y, ExponentialSmoothingOptions options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2013) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
