∇Z←dm∆Bspline∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ B-spline design factory, analogous to R's splines::bs(). Owns a clamped basis on fixed boundaries, reused for training and prediction. By default the first basis column is omitted, so a formula's intercept does not duplicate the partition of unity. No fitting or smoothing is performed. Const evaluations are independent and safe to run concurrently.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const dm::Bspline basis(0, 1, {0, 0.5, 1});
⍝ const auto design = basis.eval({0, 0.5, 1});
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n", design.rows(), design.cols()); // 3 4
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - C. de Boor (1972). "On calculating with B-splines". Journal of Approximation
⍝   Theory 6(1), 50-62. doi:10.1016/0021-9045(72)90080-9.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('Bspline' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆Bspline∆new lower upper knots
⍝ obj←dm∆Bspline∆new lower upper knots degree
⍝ obj←dm∆Bspline∆new lower upper knots degree intercept
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Build a clamped basis from strictly increasing knot breakpoints.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `lower` number: Finite left boundary, strictly below upper.
⍝ - `upper` number: Finite right boundary.
⍝ - `knots` numeric vector: Finite increasing breakpoints inside [lower, upper]; boundary entries are optional and ignored when building interior knots. May be empty.
⍝ - `degree` integer, default 3: Polynomial degree, default 3 (cubic).
⍝ - `intercept` boolean (0 or 1), default 0: Include the first basis column, default false; use a no-intercept formula when true. Column count is interior knots + degree + (intercept ? 1 : 0).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Bspline handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: For invalid boundaries/knots or overflowing degree. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::Bspline::Bspline(double lower, double upper, const std::vector<double> & knots, std::size_t degree = 3, bool intercept = false)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2014) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆BSplineRegression∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A least-squares B-spline regression curve y ≈ Σ_j β_j B_j(x). `dm::BSR` for short.
⍝
⍝ The fit is ordinary least squares (no roughness penalty). Throws std::invalid_argument for
⍝ mismatched/empty inputs or too few basis functions for the degree, and std::runtime_error when
⍝ the design is rank deficient (some basis function has too little data under it; use fewer
⍝ basis functions / knots).
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆BSplineRegression∆predict`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆coefficients`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆fitted`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆residuals`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆r_squared`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆basis_size`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆degree`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆knots`, `dm∆BSplineRegression∆domain`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('BSplineRegression' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆BSplineRegression∆new x y n_basis
⍝ obj←dm∆BSplineRegression∆new x y n_basis degree
⍝ obj←dm∆BSplineRegression∆new x y knots
⍝ obj←dm∆BSplineRegression∆new x y knots degree
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Fixed-width basis: `n_basis` B-splines of the given `degree` (cubic by default) whose knots are equally spaced over the range of `x`.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** BSplineRegression handle
