∇Z←dm∆CsvReader∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly streaming CSV reader: returns a big file as DataFrames of at most batch_size() rows each, so only one chunk is in memory at a time.
⍝
⍝ Wraps datasets::CsvReader; column types are fixed from the first 1000 rows.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::CsvReader reader(dm::datasets::fetch("diamonds"), 10000);
⍝ while (reader.has_next()) {
⍝   std::unique_ptr<dm::DataFrame> chunk(reader.next());
⍝   // ... use chunk ...
⍝ }
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆CsvReader∆has_next`, `dm∆CsvReader∆next`, `dm∆CsvReader∆reset`, `dm∆CsvReader∆batch_size`, `dm∆CsvReader∆set_batch_size`, `dm∆CsvReader∆column_names`, `dm∆CsvReader∆rows_read`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('CsvReader' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆CsvReader∆new path
⍝ obj←dm∆CsvReader∆new path batch_size
⍝ obj←dm∆CsvReader∆new path batch_size delimiter
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Opens `path` and infers its column types.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `path` character vector: The CSV file.
⍝ - `batch_size` integer, default 1000: Rows per chunk; must be positive.
⍝ - `delimiter` character, default ',': The field separator.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** CsvReader handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: if batch_size is not positive. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: if the file cannot be opened or is malformed. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::CsvReader::CsvReader(const std::string & path, int batch_size = 1000, char delimiter = ',')`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2106) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

