∇Z←dm∆GGPlot∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::graphics::GGPlot — a ggplot2-style grammar-of-graphics builder. Geom/theme/scale/facet calls are chainable, mirroring ggplot2's own layered `ggplot(df, aes(...)) + geom_point() + ...` style as closely as C++ method chaining allows.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_point`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_line`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_bar`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_col`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_histogram`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_boxplot`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_smooth`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_area`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_ribbon`, `dm∆GGPlot∆geom_density`, `dm∆GGPlot∆facet_wrap`, `dm∆GGPlot∆theme_minimal`, `dm∆GGPlot∆theme_bw`, `dm∆GGPlot∆theme_classic`, `dm∆GGPlot∆scale_color_manual`, `dm∆GGPlot∆labs`, `dm∆GGPlot∆to_svg`, `dm∆GGPlot∆save`, `dm∆GGPlot∆save_svg`, `dm∆GGPlot∆show`, `dm∆GGPlot∆rows`, `dm∆GGPlot∆x_column`, `dm∆GGPlot∆y_column`, `dm∆GGPlot∆color_column`, `dm∆GGPlot∆layer_count`, `dm∆GGPlot∆layer_kinds`, `dm∆GGPlot∆theme_name`, `dm∆GGPlot∆facet_column`, `dm∆GGPlot∆title_text`, `dm∆GGPlot∆x_label`, `dm∆GGPlot∆y_label`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('GGPlot' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆GGPlot∆new data x_column
⍝ obj←dm∆GGPlot∆new data x_column y_column
⍝ obj←dm∆GGPlot∆new data x_column y_column color_column
⍝ obj←dm∆GGPlot∆new data x_column y_column color_column fill_column
⍝ obj←dm∆GGPlot∆new data x_column y_column color_column fill_column group_column
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `x_column` character vector
⍝ - `y_column` character vector, default ''
⍝ - `color_column` character vector, default ''
⍝ - `fill_column` character vector, default ''
⍝ - `group_column` character vector, default ''
⍝
⍝ **Result:** GGPlot handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::GGPlot::GGPlot(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & x_column, const std::string & y_column = "", const std::string & color_column = "", const std::string & fill_column = "", const std::string & group_column = "")`
