∇Z←H dm∆Splom∆group_by B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Splits every numeric panel by the groups of string column `column` (GGally's `ggpairs(aes(colour = group))`); an empty palette uses the default level palette.
⍝
⍝ The column need not be a panel variable but must be a string column of the source
⍝ frame. Groups are its sorted distinct non-missing values, and group k takes
⍝ `palette[k % palette.size()]`. Each group gets its own points, diagonal density, smooth
⍝ and prediction band, and density contours; rows with a missing group are left out of
⍝ those panels. When the column is also a panel variable its violins, bars, and mosaic axis
⍝ share the colors. Pass "" to clear the grouping. Clears point_colors().
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto pairs = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).group_by("Species");
⍝ std::print("{}\n", pairs.groups());  // ["setosa", "versicolor", "virginica"]
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆Splom∆group_by column
⍝ Z←obj dm∆Splom∆group_by column palette
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `column` character vector: String column to group by, or "" to clear.
⍝ - `palette` vector of (RGB handle), default the C++ default: Group colors in sorted-group order; empty uses the default.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Splom handle: This matrix, for chaining.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If `column` is not a string column of the source frame. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `Splom & datamunge::Splom::group_by(const std::string & column, const std::vector<datamunge::graphics::RGB> & palette = {})`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆groups()`, `dm∆set_col()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(2156 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

