∇Z←H dm∆Splom∆panel B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Builds the panel with variable `col` on x and variable `row` on y.
⍝
⍝ The panel is a standalone dm::Plot sized to one grid cell, useful for inspecting or
⍝ saving a single pair. Indices are zero-based positions in variables().
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto pairs = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris(), {"Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width"});
⍝ pairs.panel(1, 0).save("sepal_scatter.svg");  // Sepal.Length on x, Sepal.Width on y
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆Splom∆panel row col
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `row` integer: Zero-based index of the y variable.
⍝ - `col` integer: Zero-based index of the x variable; equal to `row` gives the diagonal panel.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** RPlot handle: The rendered-on-demand panel plot.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: If either index is not below variables().size(). (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If the panel has no complete rows to draw. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::graphics::RPlot datamunge::Splom::panel(std::size_t row, std::size_t col) const`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(2172 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆Splom∆to_svg H;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Renders the matrix as a standalone SVG document and returns it as a string.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto svg = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).set_title("Iris Pairs").to_svg();
⍝ std::print("{}\n", svg.contains("Iris Pairs"));  // true
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆Splom∆to_svg obj
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Result:** character vector: The complete SVG text of the full grid, including the title band.
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::string datamunge::Splom::to_svg() const`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(2173 2 H) dm⍙native ⍬
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆Splom∆save B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Writes the matrix to `path`, choosing the format from the extension.
⍝
⍝ `.svg` or no extension writes to_svg(); `.png` and `.pdf` write the tiled raster the
⍝ viewer shows. Needs no display.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto pairs = dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).group_by("Species");
⍝ pairs.save("iris_pairs.svg");
⍝ pairs.save("iris_pairs.png");
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆Splom∆save path
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `path` character vector: Destination file; an existing file is overwritten.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: For any other extension. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If the file cannot be written. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::Splom::save(const std::string & path) const`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(2174 0 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆Splom∆save_svg B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
