⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::Splom::save_svg(const std::string & path) const`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(2175 0 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆Splom∆show B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Opens the matrix in the interactive X11 viewer and blocks until the window closes.
⍝
⍝ Zoom and pan act on every panel at once; q or Escape closes the window. Requires an
⍝ X11-enabled build and a reachable display; use save() in headless code.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::Splom(dm::datasets::iris()).set_title("Iris Pairs").group_by("Species").show();
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆Splom∆show ⍬
⍝ obj dm∆Splom∆show title_hint
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `title_hint` character vector, default '': Window title; empty uses the figure title, or "datamunge splom".
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If X11 is unavailable or the display cannot be opened. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::Splom::show(const std::string & title_hint = "") const`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(2176 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

