∇Z←dm∆LMM∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::LMM — a linear mixed model fit by (RE)ML, with a single grouping factor, e.g. "score ~ x1 + (1 + x1 | school)".
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆LMM∆formula_text`, `dm∆LMM∆group_variable`, `dm∆LMM∆has_random_intercept`, `dm∆LMM∆random_effect_names`, `dm∆LMM∆is_reml`, `dm∆LMM∆observations`, `dm∆LMM∆num_groups`, `dm∆LMM∆rank`, `dm∆LMM∆coefficients`, `dm∆LMM∆coefficient_names`, `dm∆LMM∆standard_errors`, `dm∆LMM∆z_values`, `dm∆LMM∆p_values`, `dm∆LMM∆fitted_values`, `dm∆LMM∆residuals`, `dm∆LMM∆residual_variance`, `dm∆LMM∆residual_std_dev`, `dm∆LMM∆random_effect_std_devs`, `dm∆LMM∆random_effect_correlation`, `dm∆LMM∆group_labels`, `dm∆LMM∆random_effects_for_group`, `dm∆LMM∆log_likelihood`, `dm∆LMM∆deviance`, `dm∆LMM∆aic`, `dm∆LMM∆bic`, `dm∆LMM∆summary`, `dm∆LMM∆print_summary`, `dm∆LMM∆predict`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('LMM' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆LMM∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆LMM∆new data formula reml
⍝ obj←dm∆LMM∆new data formula reml de_population_size
⍝ obj←dm∆LMM∆new data formula reml de_population_size de_max_generations
⍝ obj←dm∆LMM∆new data formula reml de_population_size de_max_generations theta_bound
⍝ obj←dm∆LMM∆new data formula reml de_population_size de_max_generations theta_bound seed
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `reml` boolean (0 or 1), default 1: REML (default) or maximum likelihood.
⍝ - `de_population_size` integer, default 40
⍝ - `de_max_generations` integer, default 300
⍝ - `theta_bound` number, default 5.0: Box-constraint magnitude (relative to the residual SD) for the DifferentialEvolution search over variance-component parameters.
⍝ - `seed` integer, default 42
⍝
⍝ **Result:** LMM handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::LMM::LMM(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, bool reml = true, std::size_t de_population_size = 40, std::size_t de_max_generations = 300, double theta_bound = 5.0, std::size_t seed = 42)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2240) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
