∇Z←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::INLAMixedModel — a mixed model (same formula grammar as GLMM/LMM) fit by Integrated Nested Laplace Approximation instead of penalized quasi-likelihood/REML: a genuinely Bayesian alternative returning real posterior means/sds (including for the variance components) rather than point estimates + asymptotic standard errors. See datamunge::bayes::INLA (C++-only, not exposed to bindings -- same reasoning as AutodiffModel) for the underlying algorithm.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆formula_text`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆family`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆group_variable`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆random_effect_names`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆observations`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆num_groups`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆fixed_effects_mean`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆fixed_effects_sd`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆coefficient_names`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆random_effect_std_devs`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆residual_std_dev`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆group_labels`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆random_effects_mean_for_group`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆random_effects_sd_for_group`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆log_marginal_likelihood`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆summary`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆print_summary`, `dm∆INLAMixedModel∆predict`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('INLAMixedModel' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy fixed_effect_prior_sd
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy fixed_effect_prior_sd grid_points_per_dim
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy fixed_effect_prior_sd grid_points_per_dim grid_span
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy fixed_effect_prior_sd grid_points_per_dim grid_span mode_population_size
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy fixed_effect_prior_sd grid_points_per_dim grid_span mode_population_size mode_max_generations
⍝ obj←dm∆INLAMixedModel∆new data formula family strategy fixed_effect_prior_sd grid_points_per_dim grid_span mode_population_size mode_max_generations seed
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `family` character vector, default 'gaussian': One of "gaussian" (identity link), "binomial" (logit link), or "poisson" (log link).
⍝ - `strategy` character vector, default 'grid': One of "grid" (integrate over hyperparameter uncertainty) or "eb" (empirical Bayes: fix hyperparameters at their posterior mode).
⍝ - `fixed_effect_prior_sd` number, default 1000.0
⍝ - `grid_points_per_dim` integer, default 7
⍝ - `grid_span` number, default 4.0
⍝ - `mode_population_size` integer, default 40
⍝ - `mode_max_generations` integer, default 200
⍝ - `seed` integer, default 42
⍝
⍝ **Result:** INLAMixedModel handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::INLAMixedModel::INLAMixedModel(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, const std::string & family = "gaussian", const std::string & strategy = "grid", double fixed_effect_prior_sd = 1000.0, std::size_t grid_points_per_dim = 7, double grid_span = 4.0, std::size_t mode_population_size = 40, std::size_t mode_max_generations = 200, std::size_t seed = 42)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2285) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

