∇Z←dm∆LDA∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::LDA — R-`MASS::lda()`-style linear discriminant analysis.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆LDA∆classes`, `dm∆LDA∆predictor_names`, `dm∆LDA∆observations`, `dm∆LDA∆num_discriminants`, `dm∆LDA∆priors`, `dm∆LDA∆group_means`, `dm∆LDA∆scaling`, `dm∆LDA∆proportion_of_trace`, `dm∆LDA∆training_accuracy`, `dm∆LDA∆confusion_matrix`, `dm∆LDA∆summary`, `dm∆LDA∆print_summary`, `dm∆LDA∆to_md`, `dm∆LDA∆predict`, `dm∆LDA∆predict_frame`, `dm∆LDA∆plot_discriminants`, `dm∆LDA∆save_discriminant_plot`, `dm∆LDA∆plot_decision_regions`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('LDA' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆LDA∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆LDA∆new data formula priors
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `priors` numeric vector, default the C++ default: Optional class prior probabilities (must sum to 1, ordered as classes() once sorted alphabetically); pass an empty vector (the default) to use observed class proportions.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** LDA handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::LDA::LDA(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, const std::vector<double> & priors = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2304) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
