∇Z←dm∆ElasticNet∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::ElasticNet — regularized linear regression fit by coordinate descent (alpha=0 is ridge, alpha=1 is lasso); see also the Ridge and Lasso convenience facades below.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆ElasticNet∆formula_text`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆has_intercept`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆predictor_names`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆observations`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆alpha`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆lambda`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆lambda_was_selected`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆lambda_path`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆cv_mean_squared_error`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆coefficients`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆intercept`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆non_zero_coefficients`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆fitted_values`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆residuals`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆r_squared`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆rmse`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆summary`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆print_summary`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆predict`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆plot_coefficient_path`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆plot_cv_curve`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆plot_predicted_vs_actual`, `dm∆ElasticNet∆plot_residuals_vs_fitted`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('ElasticNet' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula alpha
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula alpha lambda
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula alpha lambda n_lambda
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula alpha lambda n_lambda cv_folds
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula alpha lambda n_lambda cv_folds standardize
⍝ obj←dm∆ElasticNet∆new data formula alpha lambda n_lambda cv_folds standardize seed
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `alpha` number, default 0.5: L1/L2 mixing: 0 = ridge, 1 = lasso, in between = elastic net.
⍝ - `lambda` number, default ¯1.0: Regularization strength; pass a negative value (the default) to select it automatically via cross-validation.
⍝ - `n_lambda` integer, default 100
⍝ - `cv_folds` integer, default 5
⍝ - `standardize` boolean (0 or 1), default 1
⍝ - `seed` integer, default 42
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ElasticNet handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::ElasticNet::ElasticNet(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, double alpha = 0.5, double lambda = -1.0, std::size_t n_lambda = 100, std::size_t cv_folds = 5, bool standardize = true, std::uint64_t seed = 42)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 2402) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
