∇Z←dm∆Ridge∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::Ridge — pure L2-penalized ("ridge") regression, a special case of ElasticNet with alpha fixed to 0. Shrinks coefficients toward zero without ever zeroing them.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆Ridge∆formula_text`, `dm∆Ridge∆has_intercept`, `dm∆Ridge∆predictor_names`, `dm∆Ridge∆observations`, `dm∆Ridge∆lambda`, `dm∆Ridge∆lambda_was_selected`, `dm∆Ridge∆lambda_path`, `dm∆Ridge∆cv_mean_squared_error`, `dm∆Ridge∆coefficients`, `dm∆Ridge∆intercept`, `dm∆Ridge∆fitted_values`, `dm∆Ridge∆residuals`, `dm∆Ridge∆r_squared`, `dm∆Ridge∆rmse`, `dm∆Ridge∆summary`, `dm∆Ridge∆print_summary`, `dm∆Ridge∆predict`, `dm∆Ridge∆plot_coefficient_path`, `dm∆Ridge∆plot_cv_curve`, `dm∆Ridge∆plot_predicted_vs_actual`, `dm∆Ridge∆plot_residuals_vs_fitted`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('Ridge' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆Ridge∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆Ridge∆new data formula lambda
⍝ obj←dm∆Ridge∆new data formula lambda n_lambda
⍝ obj←dm∆Ridge∆new data formula lambda n_lambda cv_folds
⍝ obj←dm∆Ridge∆new data formula lambda n_lambda cv_folds standardize
⍝ obj←dm∆Ridge∆new data formula lambda n_lambda cv_folds standardize seed
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `lambda` number, default ¯1.0
⍝ - `n_lambda` integer, default 100
⍝ - `cv_folds` integer, default 5
⍝ - `standardize` boolean (0 or 1), default 1
⍝ - `seed` integer, default 42
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Ridge handle
