∇Z←dm∆KNNClassifier∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::KNNClassifier — k-nearest-neighbors classification. Since a training point's nearest neighbor is always itself, training_accuracy()/confusion_matrix() report leave-one-out performance rather than a trivial resubstitution fit.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆KNNClassifier∆classes`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆predictor_names`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆observations`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆k`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆training_accuracy`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆confusion_matrix`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆summary`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆print_summary`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆predict`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆predict_frame`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆plot_classification`, `dm∆KNNClassifier∆plot_decision_regions`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('KNNClassifier' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆KNNClassifier∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆KNNClassifier∆new data formula k
⍝ obj←dm∆KNNClassifier∆new data formula k metric
⍝ obj←dm∆KNNClassifier∆new data formula k metric weighted
⍝ obj←dm∆KNNClassifier∆new data formula k metric weighted standardize
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `k` integer, default 5
⍝ - `metric` character vector, default 'euclidean': "euclidean" (default) or "manhattan".
⍝ - `weighted` boolean (0 or 1), default 0
⍝ - `standardize` boolean (0 or 1), default 1
⍝
⍝ **Result:** KNNClassifier handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::KNNClassifier::KNNClassifier(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, std::size_t k = 5, const std::string & metric = "euclidean", bool weighted = false, bool standardize = true)`
