∇Z←dm∆KMeans∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::KMeans — k-means clustering (Lloyd's algorithm with k-means++ initialization) fit from a DataFrame and a list of numeric feature columns.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆KMeans∆feature_names`, `dm∆KMeans∆n_clusters`, `dm∆KMeans∆observations`, `dm∆KMeans∆iterations_used`, `dm∆KMeans∆labels`, `dm∆KMeans∆inertia`, `dm∆KMeans∆cluster_center`, `dm∆KMeans∆predict`, `dm∆KMeans∆summary`, `dm∆KMeans∆print_summary`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('KMeans' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data feature_columns
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data feature_columns n_clusters
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations n_init
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations n_init tolerance
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations n_init tolerance seed
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data encoded_feature_columns
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data encoded_feature_columns n_clusters
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data encoded_feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data encoded_feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations n_init
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data encoded_feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations n_init tolerance
⍝ obj←dm∆KMeans∆new data encoded_feature_columns n_clusters max_iterations n_init tolerance seed
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Same as the vector<string> constructor, but feature_columns is a single "<count> col1..."-encoded string -- a workaround for SWIG-bound languages whose overload resolution can't pass a real string vector to a constructor with other default arguments (see DataFrame::add_string_column_encoded()).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** KMeans handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::KMeans::KMeans(const DataFrame & data, const std::vector<std::string> & feature_columns, std::size_t n_clusters = 8, std::size_t max_iterations = 300, std::size_t n_init = 10, double tolerance = 1.0E-4, std::size_t seed = 42)`
