∇Z←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::GaussianProcessRegression — exact Gaussian process regression with an RBF kernel, fit via Cholesky decomposition. Unlike every other regressor here, predictions come with a principled posterior confidence interval; see predict_frame().
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆predictor_names`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆observations`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆length_scale`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆signal_variance`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆noise_variance`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆log_marginal_likelihood`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆length_scale_was_selected`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆noise_ratio_was_selected`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆length_scale_grid`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆length_scale_profile_log_likelihood`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆fitted_values`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆r_squared`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆rmse`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆summary`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆print_summary`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆predict`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆predict_frame`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆plot_fit`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆plot_predicted_vs_actual`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆plot_residuals_vs_fitted`, `dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆plot_length_scale_profile`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('GaussianProcessRegression' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new data formula
⍝ obj←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new data formula length_scale
⍝ obj←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new data formula length_scale noise_ratio
⍝ obj←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new data formula length_scale noise_ratio n_length_scale_grid
⍝ obj←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new data formula length_scale noise_ratio n_length_scale_grid n_noise_grid
⍝ obj←dm∆GaussianProcessRegression∆new data formula length_scale noise_ratio n_length_scale_grid n_noise_grid standardize
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `data` DataFrame handle
⍝ - `formula` character vector
⍝ - `length_scale` number, default ¯1.0: RBF kernel length scale in standardized-predictor units; pass a negative value (the default) to select it automatically by maximizing the log marginal likelihood.
⍝ - `noise_ratio` number, default ¯1.0: noise_variance / signal_variance; pass a negative value (the default) to select it automatically the same way (0 is a legal fixed value: a noiseless/interpolating GP).
⍝ - `n_length_scale_grid` integer, default 20
⍝ - `n_noise_grid` integer, default 15
⍝ - `standardize` boolean (0 or 1), default 1
⍝
⍝ **Result:** GaussianProcessRegression handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::GaussianProcessRegression::GaussianProcessRegression(const DataFrame & data, const std::string & formula, double length_scale = -1.0, double noise_ratio = -1.0, std::size_t n_length_scale_grid = 20, std::size_t n_noise_grid = 15, bool standardize = true)`
