∇Z←dm∆GLM∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::stats::GLM — a generalized linear model (gaussian, binomial, poisson, or Gamma family with its canonical link, matching R's glm() defaults) fit by iteratively reweighted least squares.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆GLM∆formula_text`, `dm∆GLM∆family`, `dm∆GLM∆has_intercept`, `dm∆GLM∆observations`, `dm∆GLM∆rank`, `dm∆GLM∆degrees_of_freedom`, `dm∆GLM∆coefficients`, `dm∆GLM∆coefficient_names`, `dm∆GLM∆fitted_values`, `dm∆GLM∆linear_predictors`, `dm∆GLM∆residuals`, `dm∆GLM∆pearson_residuals`, `dm∆GLM∆standardized_residuals`, `dm∆GLM∆leverage`, `dm∆GLM∆standard_errors`, `dm∆GLM∆test_statistics`, `dm∆GLM∆p_values`, `dm∆GLM∆deviance`, `dm∆GLM∆null_deviance`, `dm∆GLM∆dispersion`, `dm∆GLM∆aic`, `dm∆GLM∆confidence_interval_lower`, `dm∆GLM∆confidence_interval_upper`, `dm∆GLM∆summary`, `dm∆GLM∆print_summary`, `dm∆GLM∆predict`, `dm∆GLM∆predict_frame`, `dm∆GLM∆plot_residuals_vs_fitted`, `dm∆GLM∆plot_normal_qq`, `dm∆GLM∆plot_scale_location`, `dm∆GLM∆plot_residuals_vs_leverage`, `dm∆GLM∆save_diagnostic_plots`.
⍝
