∇Z←dm∆Dual∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::Dual -- a first-order forward-mode dual number. Build an expression out of named operations (starting from a seed with derivative=1) to read off an exact derivative alongside the value.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆Dual∆value`, `dm∆Dual∆derivative`, `dm∆Dual∆add`, `dm∆Dual∆subtract`, `dm∆Dual∆multiply`, `dm∆Dual∆divide`, `dm∆Dual∆negate`, `dm∆Dual∆add_scalar`, `dm∆Dual∆subtract_scalar`, `dm∆Dual∆multiply_scalar`, `dm∆Dual∆divide_scalar`, `dm∆Dual∆pow`, `dm∆Dual∆exp`, `dm∆Dual∆log`, `dm∆Dual∆sqrt`, `dm∆Dual∆sin`, `dm∆Dual∆cos`, `dm∆Dual∆tan`, `dm∆Dual∆tanh`, `dm∆Dual∆abs`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('Dual' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆Dual∆new value
⍝ obj←dm∆Dual∆new value derivative
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ A dual number value + derivative·ε (ε² = 0).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `value` number: Real part, the function value.
⍝ - `derivative` number, default 0.0: Dual part, the derivative with respect to the seed (default 0).
