⍝ Handles are `('HyperDual' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆HyperDual∆new value
⍝ obj←dm∆HyperDual∆new value eps1
⍝ obj←dm∆HyperDual∆new value eps1 eps2
⍝ obj←dm∆HyperDual∆new value eps1 eps2 eps1eps2
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ A hyper-dual number value + eps1·ε₁ + eps2·ε₂ + eps1eps2·ε₁ε₂ (ε₁² = ε₂² = 0).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `value` number: Real part, the function value.
⍝ - `eps1` number, default 0.0: First derivative along the first seed direction (default 0).
⍝ - `eps2` number, default 0.0: First derivative along the second seed direction (default 0).
⍝ - `eps1eps2` number, default 0.0: Mixed second derivative part (default 0; leave 0 for inputs).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** HyperDual handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::HyperDual::HyperDual(double value, double eps1 = 0.0, double eps2 = 0.0, double eps1eps2 = 0.0)`
