∇Z←H dm∆Tape∆backward B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Reverse sweep from `output`: d(output)/d(node) for every node on the tape.
⍝
⍝ The tape is unchanged, so backward() may be called again for other outputs.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::Tape tape;
⍝ const dm::Var a(tape, 2.0), b(tape, 3.0);
⍝ const auto grad = tape.backward(a.multiply(b));
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n", grad[a.index()], grad[b.index()]);  // 3 2
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆Tape∆backward output
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `output` Var handle: A Var recorded on this tape (usually the final expression).
⍝
⍝ **Result:** numeric vector: One adjoint per node, indexed by Var::index() (0-based; add 1 in R and Lua).
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: When `output` is not a node of this tape. (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<double> datamunge::Tape::backward(const Var & output) const`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(2926 0 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆CadSolid∆new B
⍝ An owned B-rep solid with value-returning modelling and export operations. Geometry uses doubles in caller-selected consistent units. Copies own topology; immutable surfaces may be shared. Operations return new solids, preserving inputs. Unsupported kernel operations throw std::runtime_error with the kernel diagnostic. Concurrent const access is safe; do not mutate a shared object concurrently.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto block = dm::cad::Solid::box(4, 3, 2);
⍝ auto hole = dm::cad::Solid::cylinder(.4, 4).translated(2, 1.5, -1);
⍝ auto part = block.subtracted(hole);
⍝ part.save("part.step");
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆CadSolid∆box` (static), `dm∆CadSolid∆cylinder` (static), `dm∆CadSolid∆sphere` (static), `dm∆CadSolid∆torus` (static), `dm∆CadSolid∆united`, `dm∆CadSolid∆subtracted`, `dm∆CadSolid∆intersected`, `dm∆CadSolid∆translated`, `dm∆CadSolid∆rotated`, `dm∆CadSolid∆filleted`, `dm∆CadSolid∆chamfered`, `dm∆CadSolid∆shelled`, `dm∆CadSolid∆volume`, `dm∆CadSolid∆valid`, `dm∆CadSolid∆edges`, `dm∆CadSolid∆faces`, `dm∆CadSolid∆save`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('CadSolid' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆CadSolid∆new ⍬
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ It has no public constructor: C++ functions return its objects.
 ('dm: binding: dm∆CadSolid has no public constructor') ⎕ES 5 4
∇

