∇Z←dm∆CadScene∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A small code-driven scene facade, exposed as CadScene in Python/R. Owns scene/camera/render controls. All operations delegate to the canonical CAD, polygon and renderer APIs; copying retains independent scene state.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::cad::View view;
⍝ view.add(dm::cad::Solid::box(2, 3, 4), "#3b82f6", "block");
⍝ view.size(640, 480); view.render("block.png");
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆CadScene∆from_file` (static), `dm∆CadScene∆from_urdf` (static), `dm∆CadScene∆set_joint`, `dm∆CadScene∆joint_names`, `dm∆CadScene∆add`, `dm∆CadScene∆primitive`, `dm∆CadScene∆size`, `dm∆CadScene∆samples`, `dm∆CadScene∆style`, `dm∆CadScene∆shadows`, `dm∆CadScene∆camera`, `dm∆CadScene∆fit`, `dm∆CadScene∆light`, `dm∆CadScene∆render`, `dm∆CadScene∆save_gltf`, `dm∆CadScene∆pick_object`, `dm∆CadScene∆object_count`, `dm∆CadScene∆triangle_count`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('CadScene' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆CadScene∆new
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ Create an empty scene with automatic camera framing.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** CadScene handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::cad::View::View()`
