∇Z←dm∆OrthantCellTree∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Dyadic 2^d-ary tree of axis-aligned boxes shared by the hierarchical splines.
⍝
⍝ Cells live in a flat vector and are addressed by id (root 0). Children are created on
⍝ demand by halving every axis; slot bit k selects the upper half of axis k.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆dimensions`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆arity`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆size`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆max_depth`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆check`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆check_slot`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆lo`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆hi`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆depth`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆parent`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆child`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆is_leaf`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆ensure_child`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆child_box`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆slot_for`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆contains`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆locate`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆cells_at_depth`, `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆overlaps` (static), `dm∆OrthantCellTree∆covered_to_depth`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('OrthantCellTree' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆OrthantCellTree∆new lo hi
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Creates the root cell [lo, hi].
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `lo` numeric vector: Lower corner.
⍝ - `hi` numeric vector: Upper corner, with lo[k] < hi[k].
⍝
⍝ **Result:** OrthantCellTree handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: On empty/mismatched/non-finite bounds, lo >= hi, or more than 20 dimensions. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::fda::detail::OrthantCellTree::OrthantCellTree(std::vector<double> lo, std::vector<double> hi)`
