∇Z←dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Classical (overlay) hierarchical B-spline in the style of Forsey and Bartels: every cell of a dyadic tree may carry its own local "detail" TensorBSpline.
⍝
⍝ evaluate(x) sums the patch of every cell on the root-to-leaf path containing x. Each
⍝ patch is evaluated in its cell's local coordinates, (x - cell_min) / (cell_max -
⍝ cell_min) in [0, 1]^d, so patch bases should span [0, 1]. Patches are independent
⍝ (no shared nested basis and no truncation); see TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline for the
⍝ THB-spline construction. Cells are identified by integer ids (root 0).
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(0, 1);              // constant patch
⍝ h.set_spline(h.root(), dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {1.0}));
⍝ h.refine(h.root(), 1, dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {2.0}));          // upper half
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n", h.evaluate({0.25}), h.evaluate({0.75}));    // 1 3
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - D. R. Forsey and R. H. Bartels (1988). Hierarchical B-spline refinement. ACM SIGGRAPH
⍝   Computer Graphics 22(4), 205-212. https://doi.org/10.1145/378456.378512
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆dimensions`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆cell_count`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆root`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆parent`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆child`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆depth`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆cell_min`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆cell_max`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆locate`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆has_spline`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆spline`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆set_spline`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆clear_spline`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆subdivide`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆refine`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆refine_region`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell_penalized`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆evaluate`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆evaluate_points`, `dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆evaluate_grid`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('HierarchicalBSpline' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆new domain_min domain_max
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ Creates a hierarchy whose root cell is [domain_min, domain_max], with no patches.
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `domain_min` numeric vector: Lower corner (length d >= 1).
⍝ - `domain_max` numeric vector: Upper corner, with domain_min[k] < domain_max[k].
⍝
⍝ **Result:** HierarchicalBSpline handle
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: On empty, mismatched or non-finite bounds, min >= max, or more than 20 dimensions. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::HierarchicalBSpline(std::vector<double> domain_min, std::vector<double> domain_max)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(¯2 1 3038) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
