∇H dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Least-squares fits a new patch on `cell` so the whole hierarchy matches `values` at `points`.
⍝
⍝ The patch explains only what is left after every other patch on the path (the
⍝ residual values - evaluate(points)), in the spirit of Forsey-Bartels editing, so pass
⍝ raw data values rather than residuals. Points are global coordinates inside the cell.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
⍝ h.fit_cell(h.root(), {b}, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {1.0, 3.0});
⍝ std::print("{}\n", h.evaluate({0.5})); // 2
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell cell bases points values
⍝ obj dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell cell bases points values options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `cell` integer: Cell id; must not already have a patch (clear_spline() first to refit).
⍝ - `bases` vector of (BSplineBasis handle): Patch bases on [0, 1], one per dimension.
⍝ - `points` numeric matrix (one row per element): Sample locations inside the cell.
⍝ - `values` numeric vector: One raw data value per point.
⍝ - `options` SplineSolveOptions handle, default the C++ default: Solver settings.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: For an invalid id. (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If the cell has a patch, inputs are empty/mismatched, or a point lies outside the cell. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If the local normal equations are singular. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::fit_cell(int cell, std::vector<BSplineBasis> bases, const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const std::vector<double> & values, const SplineSolveOptions & options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(3033 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell_penalized B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Penalized (P-spline) variant of fit_cell() with per-axis `lambdas` and difference `order`; all-zero lambdas give fit_cell().
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(3, 10);
⍝ h.fit_cell_penalized(h.root(), {b}, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {0.0, 2.0}, {1e3});
⍝ std::print("{:.3f}\n", h.evaluate({0.5})); // 1.000
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell_penalized cell bases points values lambdas
⍝ obj dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell_penalized cell bases points values lambdas order
⍝ obj dm∆HierarchicalBSpline∆fit_cell_penalized cell bases points values lambdas order options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `cell` integer: Cell id without a patch.
⍝ - `bases` vector of (BSplineBasis handle): Patch bases on [0, 1].
⍝ - `points` numeric matrix (one row per element): Sample locations inside the cell.
⍝ - `values` numeric vector: Raw data values.
⍝ - `lambdas` numeric vector: Nonnegative per-axis weights.
⍝ - `order` integer, default 2: Difference order (default 2).
⍝ - `options` SplineSolveOptions handle, default the C++ default: Solver settings.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: For an invalid id. (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: As for fit_cell() and fit_tensor_pspline(). (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If the penalized normal equations are singular. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline::fit_cell_penalized(int cell, std::vector<BSplineBasis> bases, const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const std::vector<double> & values, const std::vector<double> & lambdas, int order = 2, const SplineSolveOptions & options = {})`
