∇Z←H dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆refine B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Creates (if needed) the child of `cell` at `slot`, materializing the next level when first reached. The represented function is unchanged.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
⍝ dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 1.0}));
⍝ thb.refine(thb.root(), 0);
⍝ std::print("{} {}\n", thb.level_count(), thb.evaluate({0.25})); // 2 0.25
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆refine cell slot
⍝ ```
