∇H dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆set_coefficient B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Sets the coefficient of an active function and propagates the change, with truncation, to every finer level. The edit is local to the function's support.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
⍝ dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 0.0}));
⍝ thb.set_coefficient(0, {1}, 2.0);
⍝ std::print("{}\n", thb.evaluate({0.5})); // 1
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆set_coefficient level index value
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `level` integer: Level.
⍝ - `index` integer vector: Active multi-index.
⍝ - `value` number: New coefficient.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: For invalid levels/indices. (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: On a dimension mismatch or an inactive index. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::set_coefficient(int level, const std::vector<int> & index, double value)`
