⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
⍝ dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 1.0}));
⍝ std::print("{}\n", thb.truncated_basis(0, {1}, {0.25})); // 0.25
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆truncated_basis level index point
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `level` integer: Level.
⍝ - `index` integer vector: Multi-index (inactive functions give 0).
⍝ - `point` numeric vector: d coordinates inside the domain.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** number: Truncated basis value.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: For invalid levels/indices. (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: On a size mismatch or a point outside the domain. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
