∇H dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_level_penalized B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Penalized variant of fit_level(): adds the level's full-grid tensor difference penalty restricted to its active functions, applied to the coefficient change.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(3, 8);
⍝ dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, std::vector<double>(8, 0.0)));
⍝ thb.fit_level_penalized(0, {{0.0}, {1.0}}, {0.0, 1.0}, {1e3});
⍝ std::print("{:.3f}\n", thb.evaluate({0.5})); // 0.500
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_level_penalized level points values lambdas
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_level_penalized level points values lambdas order
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_level_penalized level points values lambdas order options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `level` integer: Level.
⍝ - `points` numeric matrix (one row per element): Sample locations.
⍝ - `values` numeric vector: Raw values.
⍝ - `lambdas` numeric vector: Nonnegative per-axis weights.
⍝ - `order` integer, default 2: Difference order (default 2).
⍝ - `options` SplineSolveOptions handle, default the C++ default: Solver settings.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - INDEX ERROR `dm: out_of_range: …`: For an invalid level. (C++ `std::out_of_range`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: As for fit_level() and tensor_difference_penalty(). (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If the normal equations are singular. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit_level_penalized(int level, const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const std::vector<double> & values, const std::vector<double> & lambdas, int order = 2, const SplineSolveOptions & options = {})`
