∇H dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Least-squares fit of every active coefficient on every level at once (replaces the current function).
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(1, 2);
⍝ dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {0.0, 0.0}));
⍝ thb.refine(thb.root(), 1);                      // adds a knot at 0.5
⍝ thb.fit({{0.0}, {0.25}, {0.5}, {0.75}, {1.0}}, {1.0, 0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0}); // |2x - 1|
⍝ std::print("{:.3f}\n", thb.evaluate({0.75})); // 0.500
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit points values
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit points values options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `points` numeric matrix (one row per element): Sample locations inside the domain.
⍝ - `values` numeric vector: One value per point.
⍝ - `options` SplineSolveOptions handle, default the C++ default: Solver settings.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: On empty/mismatched inputs or points outside the domain. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If some active function has too little data (singular). (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit(const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const std::vector<double> & values, const SplineSolveOptions & options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(3063 1 H) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇H dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_penalized B;⍙M;⍙E;⍙Z
⍝ Penalized all-level fit: adds lambda_k times the squared order-q differences along axis k of every run of q + 1 neighbouring active coefficients of a level.
⍝
⍝ Differences that would involve an inactive coefficient are omitted, so for q >= 1
⍝ constant coefficients (and, generally, polynomials of degree < q in the coefficient
⍝ index on each level) are unpenalized; q = 0 is ridge regression on all coefficients.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(2, 6);
⍝ dm::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline thb(dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, std::vector<double>(6, 0.0)));
⍝ thb.refine_region({0.0}, {0.5}, 1);
⍝ thb.fit_penalized({{0.0}, {1.0}}, {2.0, 2.0}, {1.0}, 1);
⍝ std::print("{:.3f}\n", thb.evaluate({0.3})); // 2.000
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_penalized points values lambdas
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_penalized points values lambdas order
⍝ obj dm∆TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline∆fit_penalized points values lambdas order options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `points` numeric matrix (one row per element): Sample locations.
⍝ - `values` numeric vector: One value per point.
⍝ - `lambdas` numeric vector: Nonnegative per-axis weights.
⍝ - `order` integer, default 2: Difference order (default 2).
⍝ - `options` SplineSolveOptions handle, default the C++ default: Solver settings.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: As for fit() and tensor_difference_penalty(). (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: native: …`: If the normal equations are singular. (C++ `std::runtime_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `void datamunge::fda::TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline::fit_penalized(const std::vector<std::vector<double>> & points, const std::vector<double> & values, const std::vector<double> & lambdas, int order = 2, const SplineSolveOptions & options = {})`
 (⍙M ⍙E ⍙Z)←(3064 1 H) dm⍙native B
