∇Z←dm∆NnModel∆new B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ A sequential network. Layers are added by spec and own parameters named "<kind><index>/..." (e.g. "dense0/W", "conv1/b"); batch-norm moving statistics live in a second store. Parameters are created on the first forward pass, when the input width is known.
⍝
⍝ **Members:** `dm∆NnModel∆add_dense`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_conv2d`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_max_pool2d`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_avg_pool2d`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_global_avg_pool2d`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_batch_norm`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_layer_norm`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_dropout`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_activation`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_flatten`, `dm∆NnModel∆add_reshape`, `dm∆NnModel∆num_layers`, `dm∆NnModel∆summary`, `dm∆NnModel∆forward`, `dm∆NnModel∆predict`, `dm∆NnModel∆loss`, `dm∆NnModel∆compute_gradients`, `dm∆NnModel∆gradient`, `dm∆NnModel∆set_optimizer`, `dm∆NnModel∆train_step`, `dm∆NnModel∆parameter_names`, `dm∆NnModel∆parameter`, `dm∆NnModel∆set_parameter`, `dm∆NnModel∆parameter_count`, `dm∆NnModel∆save`, `dm∆NnModel∆load`.
⍝
⍝ Handles are `('NnModel' id)`; release them with `dm∆Delete obj`.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ obj←dm∆NnModel∆new ⍬
⍝ obj←dm∆NnModel∆new seed
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `seed` integer, default 0
⍝
⍝ **Result:** NnModel handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `datamunge::nn::NnModel::NnModel(unsigned int seed = 0)`
