⍝ - `f` Expr handle
⍝ - `var` character vector
⍝ - `a` number
⍝ - `b` number
⍝ - `tolerance` number, default 1.0000000000000001E¯9: Target absolute error per the adaptive refinement's own error estimate; not a hard guarantee for a pathological (e.g. discontinuous or highly oscillatory) integrand.
⍝ - `max_depth` integer, default 50: Hard cap on recursive bisection depth, bounding worst-case cost.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** number
⍝
⍝ - C++: `double datamunge::algebra::definite_integral(const Expr & f, const std::string & var, double a, double b, double tolerance = 1.0000000000000001E-9, int max_depth = 50)`
