∇Z←dm∆extract_local_maxima B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Keeps only the response-field entries that are a strict local maximum within a (2*radius+1)^2 window AND exceed `threshold`, as a sorted-by-descending-response Corner list -- the standard non-max-suppression + thresholding pass shared by every response-map-based corner detector.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆extract_local_maxima response width height threshold nms_radius
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `response` numeric vector
⍝ - `width` integer
⍝ - `height` integer
⍝ - `threshold` number
⍝ - `nms_radius` integer
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (Corner handle)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<Corner> datamunge::cv::detail::extract_local_maxima(const std::vector<double> & response, int width, int height, double threshold, int nms_radius)`
