 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆harris_corners B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Harris corner detection: response = det(M) - k*trace(M)^2 of the structure tensor M at every pixel, thresholded at `threshold_ratio` * (the response map's own max, so callers don't have to guess an absolute scale) and non-max-suppressed within a (2*nms_radius+1)^2 window. `k` is the classical Harris free parameter (0.04-0.06).
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆harris_corners img
⍝ Z←dm∆harris_corners img k
⍝ Z←dm∆harris_corners img k sigma
⍝ Z←dm∆harris_corners img k sigma threshold_ratio
⍝ Z←dm∆harris_corners img k sigma threshold_ratio nms_radius
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `img` Image handle
⍝ - `k` number, default 0.040000000000000001
⍝ - `sigma` number, default 1.0
⍝ - `threshold_ratio` number, default 0.01
⍝ - `nms_radius` integer, default 3
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (Corner handle)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<Corner> datamunge::cv::harris_corners(const image::Image & img, double k = 0.040000000000000001, double sigma = 1.0, double threshold_ratio = 0.01, int nms_radius = 3)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(71 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆shi_tomasi_corners B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Shi-Tomasi ("good features to track") corner detection: response = the structure tensor's SMALLER eigenvalue at every pixel (a corner needs strong gradient variation in BOTH directions, so the weaker direction is the limiting factor) -- otherwise identical thresholding/NMS pipeline to harris_corners().
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆shi_tomasi_corners img
⍝ Z←dm∆shi_tomasi_corners img sigma
⍝ Z←dm∆shi_tomasi_corners img sigma threshold_ratio
⍝ Z←dm∆shi_tomasi_corners img sigma threshold_ratio nms_radius
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `img` Image handle
⍝ - `sigma` number, default 1.0
⍝ - `threshold_ratio` number, default 0.01
⍝ - `nms_radius` integer, default 3
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (Corner handle)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<Corner> datamunge::cv::shi_tomasi_corners(const image::Image & img, double sigma = 1.0, double threshold_ratio = 0.01, int nms_radius = 3)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(72 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆fast_corners B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ FAST corner detection: a pixel is a corner if `min_contiguous` (out of 16) pixels on the Bresenham circle of radius 3 around it are ALL brighter than center+ `threshold` or ALL darker than center- `threshold`. This is the direct O(16) full-circle test (no accelerated high-speed pre-rejection on pixels 1/5/9/13) -- simpler to verify correct, at the cost of the constant-factor speed FAST is normally chosen for. Response is the found arc's mean absolute deviation from the center intensity.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆fast_corners img
⍝ Z←dm∆fast_corners img threshold
⍝ Z←dm∆fast_corners img threshold min_contiguous
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `img` Image handle
⍝ - `threshold` integer, default 20
⍝ - `min_contiguous` integer, default 9
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (Corner handle)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<Corner> datamunge::cv::fast_corners(const image::Image & img, int threshold = 20, int min_contiguous = 9)`
