∇Z←dm∆erode B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Binary erosion: a pixel stays foreground (luma >= 128, matching image::threshold()'s convention) only if EVERY pixel within the structuring element centered on it is also foreground -- shrinks foreground regions and removes thin protrusions. Returns a Grayscale image with 0/255 values. Pixels outside the image count as background.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆erode img
⍝ Z←dm∆erode img se
⍝ Z←dm∆erode img se radius
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `img` Image handle
⍝ - `se` integer (dm∆StructuringElement∆…, or the enumerator's name), default dm∆StructuringElement∆Square
⍝ - `radius` integer, default 1
⍝
⍝ **Result:** Image handle
⍝
⍝ - C++: `image::Image datamunge::cv::erode(const image::Image & img, StructuringElement se = Square, int radius = 1)`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(79 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆dilate B;⍙M;⍙E
