∇Z←dm∆make_rectangular_mesh2d B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Builds a structured rectangular mesh on [x0, x1] x [y0, y1]: nx * ny grid cells, each split into two counterclockwise triangles, for a total of nx*ny*2 triangles and (nx+1)*(ny+1) nodes, ordered row-major (x fastest, then y). Throws std::invalid_argument if nx or ny is 0, or if x1 <= x0 or y1 <= y0.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆make_rectangular_mesh2d x0 y0 x1 y1 nx ny
