∇Z←dm∆closest_pair B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Return the closest point copies and finite-double distance using the checked all-pairs kernel. Validates at least two finite points, visits every original i<j pair and compares widened hypot distances. Equal rounded distances keep the lexicographically first index pair. Duplicates are valid distinct records and can yield zero. No early stop, sorting or spatial pruning; O(n^2) work and O(1) auxiliary storage. No input mutation/shared state. Widened comparison can change former false zero/infinite results and last-bit ties; it is not an exact-real predicate. The old call/result layout remains; indexed/traced variants retain input ids.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto r=dm::geometry::closest_pair({{0,0},{3,4},{0,1}});
⍝ std::print("{}\n",r.distance); // 1
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆closest_pair points
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `points` vector of (Point2D handle): Borrowed original finite planar coordinates, length at least two.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ClosestPairResult handle: Owned selected point copies and checked finite-double measured distance.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: If point count is too small or any coordinate is nonfinite. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: If complete pair count cannot fit size_t. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: arithmetic_error: …`: If arithmetic/counters or the selected legacy distance cannot fit. (C++ `std::overflow_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `ClosestPairResult datamunge::geometry::closest_pair(const std::vector<Point2D> & points)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆closest_pair_indexed()`, `dm∆closest_pair_trace()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(124 0) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆convex_hull B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Compute Andrew's strict monotone-chain hull using exact binary64 orientation signs. Validates all coordinates before internal indexed copies or sorting; the original by-value argument copy occurs at the call boundary. Exact coordinate equality removes duplicates (including signed zero); the earliest matching original record supplies its representation. Returns lexicographic-minimum first, counterclockwise, no repeated endpoint and no collinear edge interiors. Empty/singleton/two-point/collinear outputs follow ConvexHullAnalysis. O(n log n) comparisons plus O(n) bounded exact-sign tests, O(n) scratch/output, no global state. The legacy by-value signature is retained and has no optional caps. Other geometry routines that use cross() retain their own floating contracts.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto h=dm::geometry::convex_hull({{0,0},{2,0},{2,2},{0,2},{1,1}});
⍝ std::cout << h.size(); // 4
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - A. M. Andrew (1979), Another efficient algorithm for convex hulls in two
⍝   dimensions, https://doi.org/10.1016/0020-0190(79)90072-3 .
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆convex_hull points
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `points` vector of (Point2D handle): Finite planar records, copied by value as in the original API.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (Point2D handle): Owned strict hull of the represented coordinates.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: Any nonfinite coordinate. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: Work/container size exhaustion. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<Point2D> datamunge::geometry::convex_hull(std::vector<Point2D> points)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆convex_hull_analyze()`, `dm∆convex_hull_trace()`, `dm∆orientation_sign()`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(125 0) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆convex_hull_analyze B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Execute the same exact-sign hull kernel with identities and actual work. Same ordering, degeneracy and complexity contract as convex_hull(). Full finite validation precedes the complete max_points cap and scratch allocation. No events or completed-chain snapshots are retained; event cap is ignored.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto a=dm::geometry::convex_hull_analyze({{0,0},{1,0},{2,0}});
⍝ std::cout << a.hull.size() << ' ' << a.work.distinct_points; // 2 3
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - Andrew (1979), https://doi.org/10.1016/0020-0190(79)90072-3 .
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆convex_hull_analyze points
⍝ Z←dm∆convex_hull_analyze points options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `points` vector of (Point2D handle): Finite original records; not mutated.
⍝ - `options` ConvexHullOptions handle, default the C++ default: Complete original-record cap, zero unlimited; defaults one million.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ConvexHullAnalysis handle: Owned hull, earliest original indices and actual counters.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: Nonfinite coordinate. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: Complete point cap or work/container exhaustion. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `ConvexHullAnalysis datamunge::geometry::convex_hull_analyze(const std::vector<Point2D> & points, ConvexHullOptions options = {})`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆convex_hull()`, `dm∆ConvexHullOptions`
 (⍙M ⍙E Z)←(126 1) dm⍙native B
 ⍙M ⎕ES ⍙E
∇

∇Z←dm∆convex_hull_trace B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Capture the hull kernel's actual stack events without replay or quadratic snapshots. Same computation/work as analyze, plus O(n) owned sorted records, compact test/pop/push edits and completed lower/upper chains. Positive max_events is checked online on actual records, including pushes; zero disables the cap.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto t=dm::geometry::convex_hull_trace({{0,0},{1,0}});
⍝ std::cout << t.events.size(); // 4
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - Andrew (1979), https://doi.org/10.1016/0020-0190(79)90072-3 .
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆convex_hull_trace points
⍝ Z←dm∆convex_hull_trace points options
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `points` vector of (Point2D handle): Finite original records; not mutated.
⍝ - `options` ConvexHullOptions handle, default the C++ default: Complete point and actual event caps.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** ConvexHullTrace handle: Owned actual sorted coordinates, identities, work and scan edits.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: invalid_argument: …`: Nonfinite coordinate. (C++ `std::invalid_argument`)
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: Point/event cap or work/container exhaustion. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `ConvexHullTrace datamunge::geometry::convex_hull_trace(const std::vector<Point2D> & points, ConvexHullOptions options = {})`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆convex_hull_analyze()`, `dm∆HullEvent`
