∇Z←dm∆sample_gaussian_points B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ Draw unsnapped independent standard-normal x,y pairs with a local 32-bit MT stream. Reproduces the original hull report's mt19937/normal_distribution call order, including its cached normal variate. Distribution mappings can differ between standard libraries; a seed alone does not promise portable coordinate bits. Complete count cap precedes allocation. Empty count is valid. O(count) expected work/storage; no global RNG or mutation. Finite draws are checked before return.
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ std::cout << dm::geometry::sample_gaussian_points(40,20240728).size(); // 40
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **References**
⍝ - C++ normal_distribution specification: https://eel.is/c++draft/rand.dist.norm.normal .
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆sample_gaussian_points ⍬
⍝ Z←dm∆sample_gaussian_points count
⍝ Z←dm∆sample_gaussian_points count seed
⍝ Z←dm∆sample_gaussian_points count seed max_points
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `count` integer, default 40: Number of points, default forty.
⍝ - `seed` integer, default 20240728: Local mt19937 seed, default 20240728.
⍝ - `max_points` integer, default 1000000: Complete draw cap, default one million; zero unlimited.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (Point2D handle): Owned unsnapped normal point cloud.
⍝
⍝ **Errors:**
⍝ - LENGTH ERROR `dm: length_error: …`: Complete draw cap/container exhaustion. (C++ `std::length_error`)
⍝ - DOMAIN ERROR `dm: arithmetic_error: …`: A generated coordinate is nonfinite. (C++ `std::overflow_error`)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<Point2D> datamunge::geometry::sample_gaussian_points(std::size_t count = 40, std::uint32_t seed = 20240728, std::size_t max_points = 1000000)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆convex_hull()`, `dm∆random_point_cloud()`
