∇Z←dm∆value_colors B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ One colour per value on a continuous scale, for colouring scatter points by a numeric variable (ggplot2's `scale_colour_viridis_c()`).
⍝
⍝ Each value is mapped linearly from [`z_min`, `z_max`] to the palette and rounded to the
⍝ nearest entry; values outside are clamped, NaN values get grey (190, 190, 190), and a zero
⍝ range maps everything to the middle colour. Pass the result to RPlot::points_colored().
⍝
⍝ **Example**
⍝ ```
⍝ const auto cols = dm::graphics::value_colors({0.0, 0.5, 1.0}, dm::graphics::viridis_colors(3));
⍝ std::print("{} {} {}\n", cols[0].r, cols[1].r, cols[2].r);  // 68 35 253
⍝ ```
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆value_colors values
⍝ Z←dm∆value_colors values palette
⍝ Z←dm∆value_colors values palette z_min
⍝ Z←dm∆value_colors values palette z_min z_max
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `values` numeric vector: Values to colour.
⍝ - `palette` vector of (RGB handle), default the C++ default: Colours from low to high (default viridis_colors(256)).
⍝ - `z_min` number, default the C++ default: Value of the first colour; NaN (the default) uses the smallest value.
⍝ - `z_max` number, default the C++ default: Value of the last colour; NaN (the default) uses the largest value.
⍝
⍝ **Result:** vector of (RGB handle): One colour per value.
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<RGBA> datamunge::graphics::value_colors(const std::vector<double> & values, std::vector<RGBA> palette = {}, double z_min = ..., double z_max = ...)`
⍝
⍝ **See also:** `dm∆viridis_colors()`, `dm∆points_colored()`
