∇Z←dm∆point_in_polygon B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ True if `point` lies strictly inside the simple polygon `vertices` (given in either winding order), via the standard even-odd ray-casting rule (Franklin's PNPOLY). Behavior for a point exactly on an edge is unspecified (as it is for every ray-casting implementation) -- it may be reported as inside or outside depending on which edge and floating-point rounding.
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆point_in_polygon point vertices
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `point` Point2D handle
⍝ - `vertices` vector of (Point2D handle)
⍝
⍝ **Result:** boolean (0 or 1)
⍝
⍝ - C++: `bool datamunge::geometry::point_in_polygon(const Point2D & point, const std::vector<Point2D> & vertices)`
