∇Z←dm∆polygon_centroid B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ The centroid (center of mass, assuming uniform density) of the polygon's ENCLOSED AREA -- not the average of its vertex coordinates, which is a different point for any non-regular polygon. Throws std::invalid_argument for a degenerate (zero-area, e.g. collinear or fewer-than-3-vertex) polygon, since the formula divides by the signed area.
