⍝ Draws a straight line from (x0,y0) to (x1,y1) directly onto `img` (Bresenham's integer algorithm). `thickness` > 1 stamps a (thickness x thickness) square at every line pixel -- simple, not a true round/mitered stroke, but sufficient for this module's scope. Points (and any square stamps) outside `img's` bounds are silently clipped rather than throwing, matching typical drawing-library behavior for partially-offscreen shapes.
