∇Z←dm∆unif B;⍙M;⍙E
⍝ n draws from Uniform[lower, upper).
⍝
⍝ **Usage:**
⍝ ```apl
⍝ Z←dm∆unif lower upper n
⍝ ```
⍝ The right argument is the vector of arguments (one argument may be given alone; ⍬ for none).
⍝
⍝ **Arguments:**
⍝ - `lower` number
⍝ - `upper` number
⍝ - `n` integer
⍝
⍝ **Result:** numeric vector
⍝
⍝ - C++: `std::vector<double> datamunge::apl_bindings::unif(double lower, double upper, std::size_t n)`
